window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-09-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3"]={"id":"CGL-09-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3","title":"CGL 09 OCT 2026 SHIFT 3","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000073181","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Statement: The bank has reported a 25% rise in the number of online transactions this year.<br><br>Inference:<br>A. Customers are shifting to digital banking.<br>B. The bank forced people to use online transactions. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कथन: बैंक ने इस वर्ष ऑनलाइन लेनदेन की संख्या में 25% वृद्धि की सूचना दी है।<br><br>अनुमान:<br>A. ग्राहक डिजिटल बैंकिंग की ओर बढ़ रहे हैं।<br>B. बैंक ने लोगों को ऑनलाइन लेनदेन करने के लिए मजबूर किया। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only A is a valid inference","hi":"केवल A एक वैध अनुमान है"},"2":{"en":"Only B is a valid inference","hi":"केवल B एक वैध अनुमान है"},"3":{"en":"Both A and B are valid inference","hi":"A और B दोनों वैध अनुमान हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither A nor B is valid inference","hi":"न तो A और न ही B वैध अनुमान है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A rise in online transactions shows customers moving to digital banking, so A is valid.<br>Nothing in the statement suggests force, so B is not valid.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only A is a valid inference.</b>","hi":"ऑनलाइन लेनदेन में वृद्धि दर्शाती है कि ग्राहक डिजिटल बैंकिंग की ओर बढ़ रहे हैं, अतः A वैध है।<br>कथन में ज़बरदस्ती का कोई संकेत नहीं है, अतः B वैध नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल A एक वैध अनुमान है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000073182","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dice & Cube","question":{"en":"Two different positions of the same dice are shown, the faces of which are marked with letters M, L, W, E, V and H. Which among the following figures is the CORRECT image when the dice unfolds?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0197a693-8de6-7b8d-b8ba-e84c1eaae916_EN.jpg?edu=639294373962607776\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक ही पासे की दो अलग-अलग स्थितियाँ दिखाई गई हैं, जिसके फलकों पर अक्षर M, L, W, E, V और H अंकित हैं। पासे को खोलने पर निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी आकृति सही है?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0197a693-8de6-7b8d-b8ba-e84c1eaae916_HI.jpg?edu=639294374095013611\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0197a695-2145-78e1-9b31-4245533c6b87_EN.jpg?edu=639294373962614897\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0197f955-06f0-78e3-9971-9e70160185db_HI.jpg?edu=639294374095017703\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"2":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0197a695-2145-78e1-9b31-4246f7bb9d4d_EN.jpg?edu=639294373962614897\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0197f955-06f0-78e3-9971-9e7167d45e1a_HI.jpg?edu=639294374095017703\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"3":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0197a695-2145-78e1-9b31-4247516be465_EN.jpg?edu=639294373962624806\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0197f955-06f0-78e3-9971-9e723dcc2fd8_HI.jpg?edu=639294374095026024\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"4":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0197a695-2145-78e1-9b31-4248491b7002_EN.jpg?edu=639294373962630870\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0197f955-06f0-78e3-9971-9e7386e7bf14_HI.jpg?edu=639294374095033644\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"H is adjacent to M, W (dice a) and V, L (dice b), so E is opposite H.<br>Then V and L are adjacent, so the remaining pairs are V–M and L–W.<br>Only net (C) gives E–H, V–M and L–W as opposite pairs.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Figure (3).</b>","hi":"H के आसन्न M, W (पासा a) और V, L (पासा b) हैं, अतः H के विपरीत E है।<br>V और L आसन्न हैं, अतः शेष युग्म V–M और L–W हैं।<br>केवल जाल (C) में E–H, V–M और L–W विपरीत युग्म हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): आकृति (3) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0197a693-8de6-7b8d-b8ba-e84c1eaae916_EN.jpg?edu=639294373962607776","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0197a693-8de6-7b8d-b8ba-e84c1eaae916_HI.jpg?edu=639294374095013611"],"options":{"1":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0197a695-2145-78e1-9b31-4245533c6b87_EN.jpg?edu=639294373962614897","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0197f955-06f0-78e3-9971-9e70160185db_HI.jpg?edu=639294374095017703"],"2":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0197a695-2145-78e1-9b31-4246f7bb9d4d_EN.jpg?edu=639294373962614897","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0197f955-06f0-78e3-9971-9e7167d45e1a_HI.jpg?edu=639294374095017703"],"3":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0197a695-2145-78e1-9b31-4247516be465_EN.jpg?edu=639294373962624806","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0197f955-06f0-78e3-9971-9e723dcc2fd8_HI.jpg?edu=639294374095026024"],"4":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0197a695-2145-78e1-9b31-4248491b7002_EN.jpg?edu=639294373962630870","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0197f955-06f0-78e3-9971-9e7386e7bf14_HI.jpg?edu=639294374095033644"]}}},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000073183","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Which of the following options classifies the given roll numbers based on the pattern observed?<br>Roll Numbers: 225, 227, 229, 231 [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकल्प देखे गए पैटर्न के आधार पर दिए गए रोल नंबरों का वर्गीकरण करता है?<br>रोल नंबर: 225, 227, 229, 231 [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Increasing by 1","hi":"1 से बढ़ रहे हैं"},"2":{"en":"Increasing by 2","hi":"2 से बढ़ रहे हैं"},"3":{"en":"Increasing by 3","hi":"3 से बढ़ रहे हैं"},"4":{"en":"Decreasing by 2","hi":"2 से घट रहे हैं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"225 → 227 → 229 → 231<br>Each number is 2 more than the previous one.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Increasing by 2.</b>","hi":"225 → 227 → 229 → 231<br>प्रत्येक संख्या पिछली से 2 अधिक है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2 से बढ़ रहे हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000073184","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Choose the island that does not fit. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"वह द्वीप चुनिए जो मेल नहीं खाता। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bali","hi":"बाली"},"2":{"en":"Sumatra","hi":"सुमात्रा"},"3":{"en":"Java","hi":"जावा"},"4":{"en":"Madagascar","hi":"मेडागास्कर"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Bali, Sumatra and Java are islands of Indonesia.<br>Madagascar is an island country near Africa.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Madagascar.</b>","hi":"बाली, सुमात्रा और जावा इंडोनेशिया के द्वीप हैं।<br>मेडागास्कर अफ्रीका के पास एक द्वीपीय देश है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): मेडागास्कर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000073185","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"<b>Statement:</b><br>In the past five years, the number of foreign tourists visiting historical sites in Country X has remained constant. However, the revenue from tourism has increased by 20% annually.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. The tourism department has raised entry fees for historical sites.<br>II. Tourists are spending more on services like guided tours and souvenirs. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>कथन:</b><br>पिछले पाँच वर्षों में, देश X में ऐतिहासिक स्थलों पर आने वाले विदेशी पर्यटकों की संख्या स्थिर रही है। हालाँकि, पर्यटन से होने वाला राजस्व प्रतिवर्ष 20% बढ़ा है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. पर्यटन विभाग ने ऐतिहासिक स्थलों का प्रवेश शुल्क बढ़ा दिया है।<br>II. पर्यटक गाइडेड टूर और स्मृति-चिह्न जैसी सेवाओं पर अधिक खर्च कर रहे हैं। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I अनुसरण करता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है"},"3":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II अनुसरण करता है"},"4":{"en":"Both conclusion I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Revenue may rise for many reasons (higher fees, more spending, domestic tourists, etc.).<br>The statement does not point to any one reason, so neither conclusion definitely follows.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Neither conclusion I nor II follows.</b>","hi":"राजस्व कई कारणों से बढ़ सकता है (अधिक शुल्क, अधिक खर्च, घरेलू पर्यटक आदि)।<br>कथन किसी एक कारण की ओर संकेत नहीं करता, अतः कोई भी निष्कर्ष निश्चित रूप से अनुसरण नहीं करता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II अनुसरण करता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000073186","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"The migration pattern of birds was recorded as 3, 6, 12, 24 over four intervals. What is the next number in the sequence? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पक्षियों के प्रवास का पैटर्न चार अंतरालों में 3, 6, 12, 24 दर्ज किया गया। अनुक्रम में अगली संख्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"36"},"2":{"en":"48"},"3":{"en":"30"},"4":{"en":"60"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Each term is doubled.<br>24 × 2 = 48<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 48.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद दोगुना होता है।<br>24 × 2 = 48<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 48 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000073187","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If \"ROCKET\" is written as \"18 15 3 11 5 20\", then how is \"SPACE\" coded? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि \"ROCKET\" को \"18 15 3 11 5 20\" लिखा जाता है, तो \"SPACE\" को कैसे कूटबद्ध किया जाएगा? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"19 16 1 3 5"},"2":{"en":"18 15 2 2 4"},"3":{"en":"17 14 0 1 317 14 0 1 3"},"4":{"en":"16 13 3 2 2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Each letter is written as its position in the alphabet.<br>S = 19, P = 16, A = 1, C = 3, E = 5 → 19 16 1 3 5<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 19 16 1 3 5.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर को वर्णमाला में उसके स्थान से लिखा जाता है।<br>S = 19, P = 16, A = 1, C = 3, E = 5 → 19 16 1 3 5<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 19 16 1 3 5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000073188","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"In a survey, 25 people like Tea, 20 like Coffee, and 10 like both. How many like only Tea? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक सर्वेक्षण में, 25 लोगों को चाय, 20 को कॉफ़ी और 10 को दोनों पसंद हैं। कितने लोगों को केवल चाय पसंद है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15"},"2":{"en":"10"},"3":{"en":"13"},"4":{"en":"12"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Only Tea = Tea − Both<br>= 25 − 10 = 15<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 15.</b>","hi":"केवल चाय = चाय − दोनों<br>= 25 − 10 = 15<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 15 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000073189","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"In a survey, 150 people were asked about Yoga, Meditation, and Gym. 60 do Yoga, 80 do Meditation, 50 do Gym, 30 do Yoga and Meditation, 20 do Meditation and Gym, 15 do Yoga and Gym, and 10 do all three. How many do none? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक सर्वेक्षण में 150 लोगों से योग, ध्यान और जिम के बारे में पूछा गया। 60 योग करते हैं, 80 ध्यान करते हैं, 50 जिम करते हैं, 30 योग और ध्यान करते हैं, 20 ध्यान और जिम करते हैं, 15 योग और जिम करते हैं, और 10 तीनों करते हैं। कितने लोग इनमें से कुछ नहीं करते? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15"},"2":{"en":"20"},"3":{"en":"10"},"4":{"en":"25"}},"answer":"3","solution":{},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000073190","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The population of a town increases by 10% annually.<br><br>If the present population is 60,500, what was it two years ago? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक कस्बे की जनसंख्या प्रतिवर्ष 10% बढ़ती है।<br><br>यदि वर्तमान जनसंख्या 60,500 है, तो दो वर्ष पहले यह कितनी थी? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"50,000"},"2":{"en":"49,500"},"3":{"en":"45,000"},"4":{"en":"50,413"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Population two years ago = 60500 ÷ (1.1 × 1.1)<br>= 60500 ÷ 1.21 = 50,000<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 50,000.</b>","hi":"दो वर्ष पहले जनसंख्या = 60500 ÷ (1.1 × 1.1)<br>= 60500 ÷ 1.21 = 50,000<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 50,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000073191","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"In this sequence, what follows next: 2P, 5M, 10J, 17G, ? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"इस अनुक्रम में आगे क्या आएगा: 2P, 5M, 10J, 17G, ? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"24 F"},"2":{"en":"42 P"},"3":{"en":"26 D"},"4":{"en":"12 A"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Numbers: 1² + 1, 2² + 1, 3² + 1, 4² + 1, 5² + 1 = 26<br>Letters: P → M → J → G → D (−3)<br>Next = 26D<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 26 D.</b>","hi":"संख्याएँ: 1² + 1, 2² + 1, 3² + 1, 4² + 1, 5² + 1 = 26<br>अक्षर: P → M → J → G → D (−3)<br>अगला = 26D<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 26 D है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000073192","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, two groups of letters are related by a specific pattern. Identify the same pattern and apply it to the second group to find the missing letters.<br>ADF : WUZ :: PQR : ? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में, अक्षरों के दो समूह एक विशेष पैटर्न द्वारा संबंधित हैं। उसी पैटर्न को पहचानिए और दूसरे समूह पर लागू करके लुप्त अक्षर ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>ADF : WUZ :: PQR : ? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"KJI"},"2":{"en":"KIJ"},"3":{"en":"JKI"},"4":{"en":"JIK"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Opposite letters: A ↔ Z, D ↔ W, F ↔ U<br>WUZ = opposite of 2nd, 3rd, 1st letters of ADF.<br>PQR: opposite of Q, R, P = J, I, K → JIK<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): JIK.</b>","hi":"विपरीत अक्षर: A ↔ Z, D ↔ W, F ↔ U<br>WUZ = ADF के दूसरे, तीसरे, पहले अक्षर के विपरीत।<br>PQR: Q, R, P के विपरीत = J, I, K → JIK<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): JIK है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000073193","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option that perfectly matches the given address.<br><br>Original Address:<br>Suite No. 9C–21King’s Court Residency, Phase–IIDr. B.R. Ambedkar RoadMumbai, Maharashtra 400012India [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दिए गए पते से पूरी तरह मेल खाता है।<br><br>मूल पता:<br>Suite No. 9C–21King’s Court Residency, Phase–IIDr. B.R. Ambedkar RoadMumbai, Maharashtra 400012India [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Suite No. 9C–21King’s Court Residency, Phase-IDr. B.R. Ambedkar RoadMumbai, Maharashtra 400012India"},"2":{"en":"Suite No. 9C–21King’s Court Residency, Phase–IIDr. B.R Ambedkar RoadMumbai, Maharashtra 400102India"},"3":{"en":"Suite No. 9C–21King’s Court Residency, Phase–IIDr. B.R. Ambedkar RoadMumbai, Maharashtra 400012India"},"4":{"en":"Suite No. 9C–21King’s Court Residency, Phase–IIDr. B.R. Ambedkar RoadMumbai, Maharashtra 4000012"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"(A) has \"Phase-I\"; (B) has \"B.R\" and \"400102\"; (D) has \"4000012\" and no \"India\".<br>Only (C) matches exactly.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Suite No. 9C–21King’s Court Residency, Phase–IIDr. B.R. Ambedkar RoadMumbai, Maharashtra 400012India.</b>","hi":"(A) में \"Phase-I\"; (B) में \"B.R\" और \"400102\"; (D) में \"4000012\" है और \"India\" नहीं है।<br>केवल (C) पूरी तरह मेल खाता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): Suite No. 9C–21King’s Court Residency, Phase–IIDr. B.R. Ambedkar RoadMumbai, Maharashtra 400012India है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000073194","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"How many such letters are there in the word BIRD, which are in the same position as in the English alphabet? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"शब्द BIRD में ऐसे कितने अक्षर हैं जो उसी स्थान पर हैं जिस स्थान पर वे अंग्रेज़ी वर्णमाला में हैं? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"B (2) is at position 1, I (9) at 2, R (18) at 3, D (4) at 4.<br>Only D matches, so the answer is 1.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"B (2) स्थान 1 पर, I (9) स्थान 2 पर, R (18) स्थान 3 पर, D (4) स्थान 4 पर है।<br>केवल D मेल खाता है, अतः उत्तर 1 है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000073195","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>ARO, CQQ, EPS, ? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई श्रृंखला के पैटर्न का अध्ययन कीजिए और श्रृंखला में अक्षरों का अगला समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>ARO, CQQ, EPS, ? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"GOU"},"2":{"en":"GPU"},"3":{"en":"GOV"},"4":{"en":"GOT"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"1st letter: A → C → E → G (+2)<br>2nd letter: R → Q → P → O (−1)<br>3rd letter: O → Q → S → U (+2)<br>Next = GOU<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): GOU.</b>","hi":"पहला अक्षर: A → C → E → G (+2)<br>दूसरा अक्षर: R → Q → P → O (−1)<br>तीसरा अक्षर: O → Q → S → U (+2)<br>अगला = GOU<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): GOU है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000073196","section":"REASONING","topic":"Counting Figures","question":{"en":"How many triangles are there in the given figure?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019e8e62-799d-70f0-9c7e-347597aa7201_EN.jpg?edu=639294373964720074\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई आकृति में कितने त्रिभुज हैं?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019e8e62-799d-70f0-9c7e-347597aa7201_HI.jpg?edu=639294374096572903\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"40"},"2":{"en":"44"},"3":{"en":"48"},"4":{"en":"42"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Each of the 5 squares with both diagonals has 8 triangles → 5 × 8 = 40<br>Each pair of adjacent squares forms 2 more large triangles (upright and inverted) → 4 × 2 = 8<br>Total = 40 + 8 = 48<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 48.</b>","hi":"दोनों विकर्णों वाले 5 वर्गों में से प्रत्येक में 8 त्रिभुज → 5 × 8 = 40<br>आसन्न वर्गों का प्रत्येक युग्म 2 बड़े त्रिभुज (सीधा और उल्टा) बनाता है → 4 × 2 = 8<br>कुल = 40 + 8 = 48<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 48 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019e8e62-799d-70f0-9c7e-347597aa7201_EN.jpg?edu=639294373964720074","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019e8e62-799d-70f0-9c7e-347597aa7201_HI.jpg?edu=639294374096572903"]}},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000073197","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You're a nurse and notice that a patient has been given a slightly higher dose of medication than what was prescribed, but the patient shows no adverse symptoms, and the shift is about to end. What should you do? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आप एक नर्स हैं और आप देखती हैं कि एक मरीज़ को निर्धारित मात्रा से थोड़ी अधिक दवा दी गई है, लेकिन मरीज़ में कोई प्रतिकूल लक्षण नहीं हैं, और शिफ़्ट समाप्त होने वाली है। आपको क्या करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Say nothing since the patient seems fine and the shift is ending.","hi":"कुछ न कहना क्योंकि मरीज़ ठीक लग रहा है और शिफ़्ट समाप्त हो रही है।"},"2":{"en":"Document the discrepancy, inform the doctor, monitor, and hand off.","hi":"विसंगति को दर्ज करना, डॉक्टर को सूचित करना, निगरानी करना और हस्तांतरण करना।"},"3":{"en":"Quietly correct the dosage in the next round without telling anyone","hi":"किसी को बताए बिना अगले राउंड में चुपचाप खुराक ठीक कर देना"},"4":{"en":"Mention it casually to the incoming nurse without formal documentation","hi":"औपचारिक दस्तावेज़ीकरण के बिना आने वाली नर्स को यूँ ही बता देना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A medication error must be recorded and reported even if no harm is seen yet.<br>Informing the doctor, monitoring and a proper handover keep the patient safe.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Document the discrepancy, inform the doctor, monitor, and hand off..</b>","hi":"दवा की त्रुटि को दर्ज और सूचित करना ज़रूरी है, भले ही अभी कोई हानि न दिखे।<br>डॉक्टर को सूचित करना, निगरानी और उचित हस्तांतरण मरीज़ को सुरक्षित रखते हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): विसंगति को दर्ज करना, डॉक्टर को सूचित करना, निगरानी करना और हस्तांतरण करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000073198","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019ed37a-4164-76c4-a9dc-8e0bfb566f89_EN.jpg?edu=639294373965237187\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में, पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक विशेष संबंध है। दी गई उत्तर आकृतियों में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनकर प्रश्न चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर रखिए ताकि तीसरी और चौथी आकृति के बीच भी वैसा ही संबंध स्थापित हो।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019ed37a-4164-76c4-a9dc-8e0bfb566f89_HI.jpg?edu=639294374096976909\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"4"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"From the first to the second figure, the elements change their positions and the arrow turns in a fixed manner.<br>Applying the same change to the third figure gives answer figure (1).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.</b>","hi":"पहली से दूसरी आकृति में तत्व अपना स्थान बदलते हैं और तीर एक निश्चित तरीके से घूमता है।<br>तीसरी आकृति पर यही बदलाव करने से उत्तर आकृति (1) मिलती है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019ed37a-4164-76c4-a9dc-8e0bfb566f89_EN.jpg?edu=639294373965237187","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019ed37a-4164-76c4-a9dc-8e0bfb566f89_HI.jpg?edu=639294374096976909"]}},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000073199","section":"REASONING","topic":"Embedded Figures","question":{"en":"In the following question, select the alternative figure which is embedded in the given fig. (X).<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019ed4a7-a865-7589-b776-858b63d958d3_EN.jpg?edu=639294373965517433\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में, वह वैकल्पिक आकृति चुनिए जो दी गई आकृति (X) में निहित है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019ed4a7-a865-7589-b776-858b63d958d3_HI.jpg?edu=639294374097190134\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The crossing lines of figure (3) can be traced exactly at the centre of figure (X).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 3.</b>","hi":"आकृति (3) की प्रतिच्छेदी रेखाएँ आकृति (X) के केंद्र में ठीक-ठीक देखी जा सकती हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019ed4a7-a865-7589-b776-858b63d958d3_EN.jpg?edu=639294373965517433","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019ed4a7-a865-7589-b776-858b63d958d3_HI.jpg?edu=639294374097190134"]}},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000073200","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In the following question, out of the five figures marked (a), (b), (c), (d), and (e), four are similar in a certain manner. However, one figure is not like the other four. Choose the figure which is different from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019edbdc-af13-7a7c-8fa0-afa7f4fe1d9d_EN.jpg?edu=639294373965809253\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में, (a), (b), (c), (d) और (e) से चिह्नित पाँच आकृतियों में से चार किसी प्रकार समान हैं। हालाँकि, एक आकृति अन्य चार जैसी नहीं है। वह आकृति चुनिए जो बाकी से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019edbdc-af13-7a7c-8fa0-afa7f4fe1d9d_HI.jpg?edu=639294374097415276\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"b"},"2":{"en":"d"},"3":{"en":"c"},"4":{"en":"e"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"(a), (b), (c) and (e) are the same figure rotated.<br>(d) cannot be obtained by rotation, so it is different.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): d.</b>","hi":"(a), (b), (c) और (e) एक ही आकृति के घुमाए हुए रूप हैं।<br>(d) घुमाकर प्राप्त नहीं हो सकती, अतः यह भिन्न है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): d है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019edbdc-af13-7a7c-8fa0-afa7f4fe1d9d_EN.jpg?edu=639294373965809253","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019edbdc-af13-7a7c-8fa0-afa7f4fe1d9d_HI.jpg?edu=639294374097415276"]}},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000073201","section":"REASONING","topic":"Counting Figures","question":{"en":"How many triangles are there in the given figure?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019edc0c-e2a5-755a-8526-e54678e095c8_EN.jpg?edu=639294373966123385\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई आकृति में कितने त्रिभुज हैं?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019edc0c-e2a5-755a-8526-e54678e095c8_HI.jpg?edu=639294374097653988\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"34"},"2":{"en":"36"},"3":{"en":"40"},"4":{"en":"42"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Counting the small triangles first and then those formed by combining parts, systematically from the apex to the base, gives 36 triangles.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 36.</b>","hi":"पहले छोटे त्रिभुज और फिर भागों को जोड़कर बनने वाले त्रिभुज, शीर्ष से आधार तक क्रमबद्ध रूप से गिनने पर 36 त्रिभुज मिलते हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 36 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019edc0c-e2a5-755a-8526-e54678e095c8_EN.jpg?edu=639294373966123385","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019edc0c-e2a5-755a-8526-e54678e095c8_HI.jpg?edu=639294374097653988"]}},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000073202","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019eeee4-7ad4-7b42-b360-586c3c58ed07_EN.jpg?edu=639294373966441499\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में, पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक विशेष संबंध है। दी गई उत्तर आकृतियों में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनकर प्रश्न चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर रखिए ताकि तीसरी और चौथी आकृति के बीच भी वैसा ही संबंध स्थापित हो।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019eeee4-7ad4-7b42-b360-586c3c58ed07_HI.jpg?edu=639294374097901016\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"From the first to the second figure, the upper element moves down, the lower one moves up, and the inner part of the double figure is removed.<br>Applying this to the third figure gives answer figure (2).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2.</b>","hi":"पहली से दूसरी आकृति में ऊपर का तत्व नीचे और नीचे का ऊपर जाता है, तथा दोहरी आकृति का भीतरी भाग हट जाता है।<br>तीसरी आकृति पर यही लगाने से उत्तर आकृति (2) मिलती है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019eeee4-7ad4-7b42-b360-586c3c58ed07_EN.jpg?edu=639294373966441499","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019eeee4-7ad4-7b42-b360-586c3c58ed07_HI.jpg?edu=639294374097901016"]}},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000073203","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Fill in the blanks (_) using one of the following four options such that the series follows a specific pattern in the given order.<br>_ op _ mo _ n _ _ pnmop _ [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिए गए चार विकल्पों में से एक का प्रयोग करके रिक्त स्थानों (_) को इस प्रकार भरिए कि श्रृंखला दिए गए क्रम में एक विशेष पैटर्न का अनुसरण करे।<br>_ op _ mo _ n _ _ pnmop _ [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"mnpmon"},"2":{"en":"mpnmon"},"3":{"en":"nmpomn"},"4":{"en":"mnpomn"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Filling m, n, p, m, o, n gives:<br>mopn / mopn / mopn / mopn<br>The unit 'mopn' repeats.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): mnpmon.</b>","hi":"m, n, p, m, o, n भरने पर:<br>mopn / mopn / mopn / mopn<br>इकाई 'mopn' दोहराई जाती है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): mnpmon है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000073204","section":"REASONING","topic":"Embedded Figures","question":{"en":"Carefully observe Figure (X) and identify the answer figure in which Figure (X) is embedded in the same or rotated form.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019f0f75-e176-7270-a347-f5cb88d40dd5_EN.jpg?edu=639294373967128950\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आकृति (X) को ध्यान से देखिए और वह उत्तर आकृति पहचानिए जिसमें आकृति (X) समान या घुमाए हुए रूप में निहित है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019f0f75-e176-7270-a347-f5cb88d40dd5_HI.jpg?edu=639294374098423774\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The square with its diagonal and the two lines meeting on it can be traced completely in figure (2).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2.</b>","hi":"विकर्ण और उस पर मिलने वाली दो रेखाओं वाला वर्ग आकृति (2) में पूरी तरह देखा जा सकता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019f0f75-e176-7270-a347-f5cb88d40dd5_EN.jpg?edu=639294373967128950","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019f0f75-e176-7270-a347-f5cb88d40dd5_HI.jpg?edu=639294374098423774"]}},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000073205","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"What follows: BCZ, DEY, FGX, HIW, JKV, ? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आगे क्या आएगा: BCZ, DEY, FGX, HIW, JKV, ? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"LNU"},"2":{"en":"LMU"},"3":{"en":"MNU"},"4":{"en":"LMV"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"First two letters are consecutive pairs: BC, DE, FG, HI, JK, LM<br>Last letter: Z → Y → X → W → V → U (−1)<br>Next = LMU<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): LMU.</b>","hi":"पहले दो अक्षर क्रमागत युग्म हैं: BC, DE, FG, HI, JK, LM<br>अंतिम अक्षर: Z → Y → X → W → V → U (−1)<br>अगला = LMU<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): LMU है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000073206","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Stone Age","question":{"en":"Langhnaj, Devnimori, and Tarsang are major excavated Mesolithic sites located in which Indian state? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"लंघनाज, देवनीमोरी और तरसंग प्रमुख उत्खनित मध्यपाषाण स्थल किस भारतीय राज्य में स्थित हैं? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gujarat","hi":"गुजरात"},"2":{"en":"Haryana","hi":"हरियाणा"},"3":{"en":"Odisha","hi":"ओडिशा"},"4":{"en":"Kerala","hi":"केरल"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Gujarat</b><br><b>Langhnaj</b> (Mehsana), <b>Devnimori</b> and <b>Tarsang</b> are archaeological sites in <b><u>Gujarat</u></b>; Langhnaj is a key Mesolithic site with microliths and human burials.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Mesolithic tools are called <b>microliths</b>.<br>• Other Mesolithic sites: <b>Bagor</b> (Rajasthan – oldest evidence of animal domestication), <b>Adamgarh</b> (MP), <b>Bhimbetka</b>.<br>• <b>Sarai Nahar Rai</b> and <b>Mahadaha</b> (UP) have Mesolithic burials.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – गुजरात</b><br><b>लंघनाज</b> (मेहसाणा), <b>देवनीमोरी</b> और <b>तरसंग</b> <b><u>गुजरात</u></b> के पुरातात्विक स्थल हैं; लंघनाज सूक्ष्म-पाषाण उपकरणों और मानव शवाधानों वाला प्रमुख मध्यपाषाण स्थल है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मध्यपाषाण उपकरणों को <b>सूक्ष्मपाषाण (Microliths)</b> कहते हैं।<br>• अन्य मध्यपाषाण स्थल: <b>बागोर</b> (राजस्थान – पशुपालन का सबसे पुराना प्रमाण), <b>आदमगढ़</b> (म.प्र.), <b>भीमबेटका</b>।<br>• <b>सराय नाहर राय</b> और <b>महदहा</b> (उ.प्र.) में मध्यपाषाण शवाधान मिले।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000073207","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Bhakti and Sufi Movements","question":{"en":"What does the term ‘malfuzat’ primarily refer to in the context of medieval Indian Sufism? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मध्यकालीन भारतीय सूफ़ीवाद के संदर्भ में ‘मल्फ़ूज़ात’ शब्द मुख्य रूप से किसे दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Doctrinal treatises written by Sufi saints","hi":"सूफ़ी संतों द्वारा लिखे गए सैद्धांतिक ग्रंथ"},"2":{"en":"Royal edicts granting patronage to khanqahs","hi":"ख़ानक़ाहों को संरक्षण देने वाले शाही फ़रमान"},"3":{"en":"Recorded conversations and teachings of saints","hi":"संतों की संकलित वार्ताएँ और शिक्षाएँ"},"4":{"en":"Mystical poetry composed in regional languages","hi":"क्षेत्रीय भाषाओं में रचित रहस्यवादी काव्य"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Recorded conversations and teachings of saints</b><br><b>Malfuzat</b> are compilations of the <b><u>conversations and teachings of Sufi saints</u></b>, recorded by their disciples.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Famous malfuzat: <b>Fawaid-ul-Fuad</b> – conversations of <b>Nizamuddin Auliya</b>, compiled by <b>Amir Hasan Sijzi</b>.<br>• <b>Maktubat</b> – letters of Sufi saints; <b>Tazkira</b> – biographies of saints.<br>• <b>Khanqah</b> – Sufi hospice.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – संतों की संकलित वार्ताएँ और शिक्षाएँ</b><br><b>मल्फ़ूज़ात</b> सूफ़ी संतों की <b><u>वार्ताओं और शिक्षाओं</u></b> का संकलन है, जिसे उनके शिष्यों ने दर्ज किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रसिद्ध मल्फ़ूज़ात: <b>फ़वाइद-उल-फ़ुआद</b> – <b>निज़ामुद्दीन औलिया</b> की वार्ताएँ, संकलक <b>अमीर हसन सिज्ज़ी</b>।<br>• <b>मक्तूबात</b> – सूफ़ी संतों के पत्र; <b>तज़किरा</b> – संतों की जीवनियाँ।<br>• <b>ख़ानक़ाह</b> – सूफ़ी आश्रम।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000073208","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Post-Maurya Dynasties","question":{"en":"Which prominent dynasty maintained territorial control over significant sections of the ancient Silk Route? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किस प्रमुख वंश ने प्राचीन रेशम मार्ग के महत्वपूर्ण भागों पर क्षेत्रीय नियंत्रण बनाए रखा? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Kushana dynasty","hi":"कुषाण वंश"},"2":{"en":"The Maurya dynasty","hi":"मौर्य वंश"},"3":{"en":"The Shunga dynasty","hi":"शुंग वंश"},"4":{"en":"The Gupta dynasty","hi":"गुप्त वंश"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – The Kushana dynasty</b><br>The <b><u>Kushanas</u></b> ruled a vast empire from Central Asia to the Ganga plains, controlling major sections of the <b>Silk Route</b> and profiting greatly from trade.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Greatest Kushana ruler: <b>Kanishka</b>, who started the <b>Saka era (78 CE)</b>.<br>• Kushanas issued the largest number of <b>gold coins</b> in ancient India.<br>• Kanishka hosted the <b>Fourth Buddhist Council</b> in Kashmir.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – कुषाण वंश</b><br><b><u>कुषाणों</u></b> ने मध्य एशिया से गंगा मैदान तक विशाल साम्राज्य पर शासन किया और <b>रेशम मार्ग</b> के प्रमुख भागों पर नियंत्रण रखकर व्यापार से भारी लाभ कमाया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सबसे महान कुषाण शासक: <b>कनिष्क</b>, जिसने <b>शक संवत (78 ई.)</b> शुरू किया।<br>• कुषाणों ने प्राचीन भारत में सबसे अधिक <b>सोने के सिक्के</b> जारी किए।<br>• कनिष्क ने कश्मीर में <b>चौथी बौद्ध संगीति</b> आयोजित की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000073209","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Governor-General and Viceroy","question":{"en":"The \"Permanent Settlement\" of revenue in Bengal was introduced in 1793 by which Governor-General? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"बंगाल में राजस्व का \"स्थायी बंदोबस्त\" 1793 में किस गवर्नर-जनरल ने लागू किया? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lord Wellesley","hi":"लॉर्ड वेलेज़ली"},"2":{"en":"Lord Cornwallis","hi":"लॉर्ड कॉर्नवालिस"},"3":{"en":"Warren Hastings","hi":"वॉरेन हेस्टिंग्स"},"4":{"en":"Sir John Shore","hi":"सर जॉन शोर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Lord Cornwallis</b><br><b><u>Lord Cornwallis</u></b> introduced the <b>Permanent Settlement</b> in Bengal, Bihar and Odisha in <b>1793</b>, making <b>zamindars</b> owners of land with a fixed revenue demand.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Cornwallis is called the <b>\"Father of Civil Services\"</b> in India.<br>• <b>Sir John Shore</b> assisted in planning the Permanent Settlement.<br>• <b>Sunset Law</b>: zamindars had to pay revenue by sunset of the fixed date or lose land.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – लॉर्ड कॉर्नवालिस</b><br><b><u>लॉर्ड कॉर्नवालिस</u></b> ने <b>1793</b> में बंगाल, बिहार और ओडिशा में <b>स्थायी बंदोबस्त</b> लागू किया, जिसमें <b>ज़मींदारों</b> को निश्चित राजस्व माँग के साथ भूमि का स्वामी बनाया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कॉर्नवालिस को भारत में <b>\"सिविल सेवा का जनक\"</b> कहा जाता है।<br>• <b>सर जॉन शोर</b> ने स्थायी बंदोबस्त की योजना में सहायता की।<br>• <b>सूर्यास्त नियम</b>: ज़मींदारों को निर्धारित तिथि के सूर्यास्त तक राजस्व देना होता था, अन्यथा भूमि छिन जाती थी।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000073210","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"As per Article 72 of the Indian Constitution, what is the meaning of the 'commutation' power granted to the President of India? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 72 के अनुसार भारत के राष्ट्रपति को दी गई 'लघुकरण' शक्ति का क्या अर्थ है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Postponing the execution","hi":"निष्पादन को स्थगित करना"},"2":{"en":"Temporary suspension of sentence","hi":"दंड का अस्थायी निलंबन"},"3":{"en":"Substituting a lighter punishment form","hi":"हल्के प्रकार के दंड से प्रतिस्थापन"},"4":{"en":"Complete acquittal of the convict","hi":"दोषी की पूर्ण दोषमुक्ति"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Substituting a lighter punishment form</b><br><b>Commutation</b> means <b><u>substituting one form of punishment with a lighter form</u></b>, e.g., death sentence commuted to rigorous imprisonment.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Pardon</b> – removes sentence and conviction; <b>Remission</b> – reduces period without changing its nature.<br>• <b>Respite</b> – lesser punishment due to special facts; <b>Reprieve</b> – stay of execution.<br>• Governor's pardoning power is under <b>Article 161</b> (cannot pardon death sentence).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – हल्के प्रकार के दंड से प्रतिस्थापन</b><br><b>लघुकरण (Commutation)</b> का अर्थ है <b><u>दंड के एक रूप को हल्के रूप से प्रतिस्थापित करना</u></b>, जैसे मृत्युदंड को कठोर कारावास में बदलना।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>क्षमा</b> – दंड और दोषसिद्धि दोनों हटाना; <b>परिहार</b> – प्रकृति बदले बिना अवधि घटाना।<br>• <b>विराम</b> – विशेष तथ्यों के कारण कम दंड; <b>प्रविलंबन</b> – निष्पादन पर रोक।<br>• राज्यपाल की क्षमा शक्ति <b>अनुच्छेद 161</b> में है (मृत्युदंड क्षमा नहीं कर सकते)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000073211","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Centre-State Relations","question":{"en":"Which Article of Indian Constitution provides for the formation of an Inter-State Council in India? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का कौन-सा अनुच्छेद भारत में अंतर-राज्य परिषद के गठन का प्रावधान करता है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 261","hi":"अनुच्छेद 261"},"2":{"en":"Article 263","hi":"अनुच्छेद 263"},"3":{"en":"Article 265","hi":"अनुच्छेद 265"},"4":{"en":"Article 267","hi":"अनुच्छेद 267"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Article 263</b><br><b><u>Article 263</u></b> empowers the President to establish an <b>Inter-State Council</b> to inquire into and advise on inter-state disputes and matters of common interest.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It was set up in <b>1990</b> on the recommendation of the <b>Sarkaria Commission</b>.<br>• <b>Art. 261</b> – full faith and credit to public acts; <b>Art. 265</b> – no tax without authority of law.<br>• <b>Art. 267</b> – Contingency Fund of India.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अनुच्छेद 263</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 263</u></b> राष्ट्रपति को अंतर-राज्यीय विवादों और साझा हितों के विषयों पर जाँच और सलाह हेतु <b>अंतर-राज्य परिषद</b> स्थापित करने का अधिकार देता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसका गठन <b>1990</b> में <b>सरकारिया आयोग</b> की सिफारिश पर हुआ।<br>• <b>अनु. 261</b> – सार्वजनिक कार्यों को पूर्ण विश्वास और मान्यता; <b>अनु. 265</b> – विधि के प्राधिकार के बिना कोई कर नहीं।<br>• <b>अनु. 267</b> – भारत की आकस्मिकता निधि।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000073212","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Supreme Court and High Court","question":{"en":"Which dispute falls under the 'Original Jurisdiction' of the Supreme Court under Article 131 of Indian constitution? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 131 के तहत कौन-सा विवाद सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के 'मूल क्षेत्राधिकार' में आता है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dispute between two private citizens","hi":"दो निजी नागरिकों के बीच विवाद"},"2":{"en":"Dispute between Center and States","hi":"केंद्र और राज्यों के बीच विवाद"},"3":{"en":"Dispute regarding the local elections","hi":"स्थानीय चुनावों से संबंधित विवाद"},"4":{"en":"Dispute involving the criminal appeals","hi":"आपराधिक अपीलों से संबंधित विवाद"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Dispute between Center and States</b><br>Under <b>Article 131</b>, the Supreme Court has exclusive original jurisdiction over <b><u>disputes between the Centre and one or more States</u></b>, or between States.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Disputes arising from <b>pre-Constitution treaties</b> are excluded.<br>• Inter-state <b>river water disputes</b> are excluded (Article 262).<br>• <b>Art. 132–134</b> – appellate jurisdiction; <b>Art. 143</b> – advisory jurisdiction.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – केंद्र और राज्यों के बीच विवाद</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 131</b> के तहत सर्वोच्च न्यायालय को <b><u>केंद्र और एक या अधिक राज्यों के बीच</u></b>, या राज्यों के बीच विवादों पर अनन्य मूल क्षेत्राधिकार है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>संविधान-पूर्व संधियों</b> से उत्पन्न विवाद इससे बाहर हैं।<br>• अंतर-राज्यीय <b>नदी जल विवाद</b> इससे बाहर हैं (अनुच्छेद 262)।<br>• <b>अनु. 132–134</b> – अपीलीय क्षेत्राधिकार; <b>अनु. 143</b> – सलाहकारी क्षेत्राधिकार।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000073213","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"Which zone marks the boundary between the crust and mantle? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कौन-सा क्षेत्र भूपर्पटी और मेंटल के बीच की सीमा दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gutenberg discontinuity","hi":"गुटेनबर्ग असांतत्य"},"2":{"en":"Mohorovicic discontinuity","hi":"मोहोरोविसिक असांतत्य"},"3":{"en":"Conrad discontinuity","hi":"कॉनराड असांतत्य"},"4":{"en":"Lehmann discontinuity","hi":"लेहमन असांतत्य"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Mohorovicic discontinuity</b><br>The <b><u>Mohorovičić (Moho) discontinuity</u></b> separates the <b>crust</b> from the <b>mantle</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Conrad</b> – between upper (sial) and lower (sima) crust.<br>• <b>Gutenberg</b> – between mantle and outer core (~2,900 km).<br>• <b>Lehmann</b> – between outer and inner core (~5,150 km).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मोहोरोविसिक असांतत्य</b><br><b><u>मोहोरोविसिक (मोहो) असांतत्य</u></b> <b>भूपर्पटी</b> को <b>मेंटल</b> से अलग करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>कॉनराड</b> – ऊपरी (सियाल) और निचली (सीमा) भूपर्पटी के बीच।<br>• <b>गुटेनबर्ग</b> – मेंटल और बाह्य क्रोड के बीच (~2,900 km)।<br>• <b>लेहमन</b> – बाह्य और आंतरिक क्रोड के बीच (~5,150 km)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000073214","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"What is the core principle behind the Athlete Biological Passport (ABP) used in anti-doping? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"डोपिंग रोधी कार्य में प्रयुक्त एथलीट बायोलॉजिकल पासपोर्ट (ABP) का मूल सिद्धांत क्या है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Direct detection","hi":"प्रत्यक्ष पहचान"},"2":{"en":"Genetic mapping","hi":"आनुवंशिक मानचित्रण"},"3":{"en":"Indirect monitoring","hi":"अप्रत्यक्ष निगरानी"},"4":{"en":"Dietary tracking","hi":"आहार निगरानी"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Indirect monitoring</b><br>The <b>ABP</b> works on <b><u>indirect monitoring</u></b>: it tracks selected <b>biological markers</b> of an athlete over time to reveal the effects of doping, rather than detecting the drug itself.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• ABP was introduced by <b>WADA in 2009</b>.<br>• Modules: <b>haematological, steroidal and endocrine</b>.<br>• It helps detect blood doping such as <b>EPO</b> use.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अप्रत्यक्ष निगरानी</b><br><b>ABP</b> <b><u>अप्रत्यक्ष निगरानी</u></b> पर कार्य करता है: यह समय के साथ खिलाड़ी के चयनित <b>जैविक मार्करों</b> पर नज़र रखकर डोपिंग के प्रभावों का पता लगाता है, न कि दवा का सीधे पता लगाकर।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ABP <b>WADA</b> ने <b>2009</b> में शुरू किया।<br>• मॉड्यूल: <b>रुधिर संबंधी, स्टेरॉयड और अंतःस्रावी</b>।<br>• यह <b>EPO</b> जैसी रक्त डोपिंग का पता लगाने में मदद करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000073215","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Bajrang Punia is best known for competing in which sporting discipline? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"बजरंग पुनिया मुख्य रूप से किस खेल में प्रतिस्पर्धा के लिए जाने जाते हैं? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Boxing","hi":"मुक्केबाज़ी"},"2":{"en":"Wrestling","hi":"कुश्ती"},"3":{"en":"Weightlifting","hi":"भारोत्तोलन"},"4":{"en":"Judo","hi":"जूडो"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Wrestling</b><br><b>Bajrang Punia</b> is a freestyle <b><u>wrestler</u></b> who won <b>bronze at Tokyo 2020</b> in the 65 kg category.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• He is the only Indian wrestler with <b>four World Championship medals</b>.<br>• He received the <b>Major Dhyan Chand Khel Ratna (2019)</b>.<br>• He won gold at the <b>2018 Asian Games and 2018 CWG</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – कुश्ती</b><br><b>बजरंग पुनिया</b> फ्रीस्टाइल <b><u>पहलवान</u></b> हैं, जिन्होंने <b>टोक्यो 2020</b> में 65 kg वर्ग में <b>कांस्य</b> जीता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वे <b>चार विश्व चैंपियनशिप पदक</b> जीतने वाले एकमात्र भारतीय पहलवान हैं।<br>• उन्हें <b>मेजर ध्यानचंद खेल रत्न (2019)</b> मिला।<br>• उन्होंने <b>2018 एशियाई खेल और 2018 राष्ट्रमंडल खेलों</b> में स्वर्ण जीता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000073216","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"The vibrant cultural festival “Putul Samaroh” is organized by which of the following states? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"जीवंत सांस्कृतिक उत्सव “पुतुल समारोह” निम्नलिखित में से किस राज्य द्वारा आयोजित किया जाता है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Madhya Pradesh","hi":"मध्य प्रदेश"},"2":{"en":"Rajasthan","hi":"राजस्थान"},"3":{"en":"Andhra Pradesh","hi":"आंध्र प्रदेश"},"4":{"en":"Himachal Pradesh","hi":"हिमाचल प्रदेश"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Madhya Pradesh</b><br><b>Putul Samaroh</b>, a <b>puppetry festival</b>, is organised by <b><u>Madhya Pradesh</u></b> (Department of Culture, Bhopal) to promote traditional puppet theatre.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Other MP festivals: <b>Khajuraho Dance Festival, Tansen Samaroh (Gwalior), Lokrang</b>.<br>• <b>Kathputli</b> (string puppetry) is famous in <b>Rajasthan</b>.<br>• Indian puppet forms: string, shadow, rod and glove puppets.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – मध्य प्रदेश</b><br><b>पुतुल समारोह</b>, एक <b>कठपुतली उत्सव</b>, <b><u>मध्य प्रदेश</u></b> (संस्कृति विभाग, भोपाल) द्वारा पारंपरिक कठपुतली रंगमंच को बढ़ावा देने के लिए आयोजित किया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• म.प्र. के अन्य उत्सव: <b>खजुराहो नृत्य समारोह, तानसेन समारोह (ग्वालियर), लोकरंग</b>।<br>• <b>कठपुतली</b> (धागा कठपुतली) <b>राजस्थान</b> में प्रसिद्ध है।<br>• भारतीय कठपुतली रूप: धागा, छाया, छड़ और दस्ताना कठपुतली।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000073217","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Why do tribal communities in Chhattisgarh traditionally perform the 'Suwa' (Parrot) dance? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"छत्तीसगढ़ के जनजातीय समुदाय पारंपरिक रूप से 'सुआ' (तोता) नृत्य क्यों करते हैं? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To please the local rain gods","hi":"स्थानीय वर्षा देवताओं को प्रसन्न करने के लिए"},"2":{"en":"To honor the spirits of ancestors","hi":"पूर्वजों की आत्माओं को सम्मान देने के लिए"},"3":{"en":"To please the Goddess of Wealth","hi":"धन की देवी को प्रसन्न करने के लिए"},"4":{"en":"To celebrate victory after a tribal war","hi":"जनजातीय युद्ध के बाद विजय का उत्सव मनाने के लिए"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – To please the Goddess of Wealth</b><br><b>Suwa Nacha</b> is performed by women of Chhattisgarh around <b>Diwali</b>, dancing around a clay parrot, <b><u>to please the Goddess of Wealth (Lakshmi)</u></b> and pray for a good harvest.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Other Chhattisgarh dances: <b>Panthi, Raut Nacha, Karma, Saila, Gendi</b>.<br>• <b>Pandavani</b> – folk ballad of Chhattisgarh by <b>Teejan Bai</b>.<br>• Suwa songs are sung by women in groups.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – धन की देवी को प्रसन्न करने के लिए</b><br><b>सुआ नाचा</b> छत्तीसगढ़ की महिलाएँ <b>दीपावली</b> के आसपास मिट्टी के तोते के चारों ओर नाचते हुए करती हैं, ताकि <b><u>धन की देवी (लक्ष्मी)</u></b> प्रसन्न हों और अच्छी फसल हो।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• छत्तीसगढ़ के अन्य नृत्य: <b>पंथी, राउत नाचा, करमा, सैला, गेंडी</b>।<br>• <b>पंडवानी</b> – छत्तीसगढ़ की लोक गाथा, प्रसिद्ध गायिका <b>तीजन बाई</b>।<br>• सुआ गीत महिलाएँ समूह में गाती हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000073218","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Which of the following traditional folk singing styles originates from Jammu and Kashmir? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी पारंपरिक लोक गायन शैली जम्मू और कश्मीर से उत्पन्न हुई है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Chhakri","hi":"छकरी"},"2":{"en":"Pandavani","hi":"पंडवानी"},"3":{"en":"Maand","hi":"मांड"},"4":{"en":"Powada","hi":"पोवाड़ा"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Chhakri</b><br><b><u>Chhakri</u></b> is a popular group folk song of <b>Kashmir</b>, sung with instruments like the noot (pot), rabab, sarangi and tumbaknari.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Pandavani</b> – Chhattisgarh; <b>Maand</b> – Rajasthan; <b>Powada</b> – Maharashtra (ballads of heroes).<br>• Kashmiri dances: <b>Rouf, Hafiza, Bhand Pather</b> (folk theatre).<br>• <b>Sufiana Kalam</b> is the classical music of Kashmir.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – छकरी</b><br><b><u>छकरी</u></b> <b>कश्मीर</b> का लोकप्रिय समूह लोकगीत है, जिसे नूट (घड़ा), रबाब, सारंगी और तुम्बकनारी जैसे वाद्यों के साथ गाया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>पंडवानी</b> – छत्तीसगढ़; <b>मांड</b> – राजस्थान; <b>पोवाड़ा</b> – महाराष्ट्र (वीरों की गाथाएँ)।<br>• कश्मीरी नृत्य: <b>रौफ़, हफ़ीज़ा, भांड पाथेर</b> (लोक नाट्य)।<br>• <b>सूफ़ियाना कलाम</b> कश्मीर का शास्त्रीय संगीत है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000073219","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Banking","question":{"en":"What is the primary objective of the \"Saa₹thi 2.0\" mobile application launched by SEBI (Securities and Exchange Board of India)? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"SEBI (भारतीय प्रतिभूति और विनिमय बोर्ड) द्वारा शुरू किए गए \"सा₹थी 2.0\" मोबाइल ऐप का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Listing of new startups on the stock exchange","hi":"स्टॉक एक्सचेंज पर नए स्टार्टअप्स की लिस्टिंग"},"2":{"en":"Empowering investors with knowledge about the securities market","hi":"निवेशकों को प्रतिभूति बाज़ार के बारे में ज्ञान से सशक्त बनाना"},"3":{"en":"Tracking real-time global commodity prices","hi":"वास्तविक समय में वैश्विक कमोडिटी कीमतों पर नज़र"},"4":{"en":"Registering complaints against fraudulent insurance agents","hi":"धोखेबाज़ बीमा एजेंटों के विरुद्ध शिकायत दर्ज करना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Empowering investors with knowledge about the securities market</b><br><b>Saa₹thi</b> is SEBI's <b>investor education app</b>; Saa₹thi 2.0 aims at <b><u>empowering investors with knowledge about the securities market</u></b> – KYC, mutual funds, trading, grievance redressal.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• SEBI's complaint portal is <b>SCORES</b>.<br>• SEBI was established in <b>1988</b>; statutory powers in <b>1992</b>; HQ <b>Mumbai</b>.<br>• The online dispute resolution platform for securities market is <b>SMART ODR</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – निवेशकों को प्रतिभूति बाज़ार के बारे में ज्ञान से सशक्त बनाना</b><br><b>सा₹थी</b> SEBI का <b>निवेशक शिक्षा ऐप</b> है; सा₹थी 2.0 का उद्देश्य <b><u>निवेशकों को प्रतिभूति बाज़ार के बारे में ज्ञान से सशक्त बनाना</u></b> है – KYC, म्यूचुअल फ़ंड, ट्रेडिंग, शिकायत निवारण।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• SEBI का शिकायत पोर्टल <b>SCORES</b> है।<br>• SEBI की स्थापना <b>1988</b> में; वैधानिक शक्तियाँ <b>1992</b> में; मुख्यालय <b>मुंबई</b>।<br>• प्रतिभूति बाज़ार का ऑनलाइन विवाद समाधान मंच <b>SMART ODR</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000073220","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Awards and Honours (Current)","question":{"en":"Which of the following pairs of book titles and language (Poetry category) for the Sahitya Akademi Award 2025 is <b>correctly</b> matched? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025 (कविता श्रेणी) के लिए पुस्तक शीर्षक और भाषा का निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा युग्म <b>सही</b> सुमेलित है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Shrestha Kabita – Dogri","hi":"श्रेष्ठ कविता – डोगरी"},"2":{"en":"Bhattkhadaki – Gujarati","hi":"भट्टखडकी – गुजराती"},"3":{"en":"Padapurana – Telugu","hi":"पदपुराण – तेलुगु"},"4":{"en":"Animesha – Odia","hi":"अनिमेषा – ओड़िया"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Bhattkhadaki – Gujarati</b><br><b><u>\"Bhattkhadaki\"</u></b> by <b>Yogesh Vaidya</b> won the <b>Sahitya Akademi Award 2025</b> in <b>Gujarati</b> (poetry). \"Shrestha Kabita\" is Bengali and \"Animesha\" is Telugu.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Bengali: <b>Prasun Bandyopadhyay</b> – \"Shrestha Kabita\".<br>• Telugu: <b>Nandini Sidha Reddy</b> – \"Animesha\".<br>• The awards (announced March 2026) carry ₹1 lakh each.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भट्टखडकी – गुजराती</b><br><b>योगेश वैद्य</b> की <b><u>\"भट्टखडकी\"</u></b> ने <b>गुजराती</b> (कविता) में <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025</b> जीता। \"श्रेष्ठ कविता\" बांग्ला और \"अनिमेषा\" तेलुगु की है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बांग्ला: <b>प्रसून बंद्योपाध्याय</b> – \"श्रेष्ठ कविता\"।<br>• तेलुगु: <b>नंदिनी सिद्धा रेड्डी</b> – \"अनिमेषा\"।<br>• पुरस्कार (मार्च 2026 में घोषित) में ₹1 लाख दिए जाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000073221","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: International Organisations","question":{"en":"Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation (BIMSTEC) is often viewed as an alternative platform for regional cooperation because of the limited effectiveness of which organization? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"बहु-क्षेत्रीय तकनीकी और आर्थिक सहयोग हेतु बंगाल की खाड़ी पहल (BIMSTEC) को किस संगठन की सीमित प्रभावशीलता के कारण प्रायः क्षेत्रीय सहयोग का वैकल्पिक मंच माना जाता है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"GCC (Gulf Cooperation Council)","hi":"GCC (खाड़ी सहयोग परिषद)"},"2":{"en":"SAARC (South Asian Association for Regional Cooperation)","hi":"सार्क (दक्षिण एशियाई क्षेत्रीय सहयोग संगठन)"},"3":{"en":"ASEAN (Association of Southeast Asian Nations)","hi":"आसियान (दक्षिण-पूर्व एशियाई राष्ट्र संघ)"},"4":{"en":"SCO (Shanghai Cooperation Organisation)","hi":"SCO (शंघाई सहयोग संगठन)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – SAARC (South Asian Association for Regional Cooperation)</b><br><b><u>SAARC</u></b> has been largely ineffective due to India–Pakistan tensions (no summit since <b>2014</b>). BIMSTEC, which excludes Pakistan, is seen as an alternative platform.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• SAARC was founded in <b>1985 at Dhaka</b>; secretariat at <b>Kathmandu</b>.<br>• The 2016 Islamabad summit was cancelled after the <b>Uri attack</b>.<br>• BIMSTEC leaders were invited to PM Modi's swearing-in in <b>2019</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सार्क (दक्षिण एशियाई क्षेत्रीय सहयोग संगठन)</b><br>भारत–पाकिस्तान तनाव के कारण <b><u>सार्क</u></b> काफ़ी हद तक निष्प्रभावी रहा है (<b>2014</b> के बाद कोई शिखर सम्मेलन नहीं)। पाकिस्तान रहित BIMSTEC को वैकल्पिक मंच माना जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सार्क की स्थापना <b>1985 में ढाका</b> में हुई; सचिवालय <b>काठमांडू</b> में।<br>• <b>उरी हमले</b> के बाद 2016 का इस्लामाबाद शिखर सम्मेलन रद्द हुआ।<br>• <b>2019</b> में प्रधानमंत्री मोदी के शपथ ग्रहण में BIMSTEC नेताओं को आमंत्रित किया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000073222","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"The office of sessions judge in a sessions division suddenly becomes vacant. An urgent bail application is pending. There is no additional sessions judge available in that division. Who may legally dispose of the application under the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किसी सत्र खंड में सत्र न्यायाधीश का पद अचानक रिक्त हो जाता है। एक तत्काल ज़मानत आवेदन लंबित है। उस खंड में कोई अपर सत्र न्यायाधीश उपलब्ध नहीं है। भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता, 2023 के तहत कौन विधिक रूप से आवेदन का निपटारा कर सकता है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only the High Court","hi":"केवल उच्च न्यायालय"},"2":{"en":"Chief Judicial Magistrate","hi":"मुख्य न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट"},"3":{"en":"Executive Magistrate","hi":"कार्यपालक मजिस्ट्रेट"},"4":{"en":"District Magistrate","hi":"ज़िला मजिस्ट्रेट"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Chief Judicial Magistrate</b><br>Under <b>BNSS</b> (old CrPC Sec. 9(6)/10(3)), when the Sessions Judge is absent or the office is vacant, an urgent application may be disposed of by an Additional or Assistant Sessions Judge, or, if none is available, by the <b><u>Chief Judicial Magistrate</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Sessions Judge is appointed by the <b>High Court</b>.<br>• The CJM is subordinate to the Sessions Judge.<br>• BNSS replaced the CrPC from <b>1 July 2024</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मुख्य न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट</b><br><b>BNSS</b> (पुरानी CrPC धारा 9(6)/10(3)) के तहत जब सत्र न्यायाधीश अनुपस्थित हो या पद रिक्त हो, तो तत्काल आवेदन का निपटारा अपर या सहायक सत्र न्यायाधीश, और यदि कोई न हो तो <b><u>मुख्य न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट</u></b> कर सकता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सत्र न्यायाधीश की नियुक्ति <b>उच्च न्यायालय</b> करता है।<br>• CJM सत्र न्यायाधीश के अधीनस्थ है।<br>• BNSS ने <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से CrPC का स्थान लिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000073223","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Awards and Honours (Current)","question":{"en":"Which award was conferred upon Justice (Retd.) Shri Jagdish Singh Khehar in 2025? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"2025 में न्यायमूर्ति (सेवानिवृत्त) श्री जगदीश सिंह खेहर को कौन-सा पुरस्कार प्रदान किया गया? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Padma Shri","hi":"पद्म श्री"},"2":{"en":"Padma Vibhushan","hi":"पद्म विभूषण"},"3":{"en":"Bharat Ratna","hi":"भारत रत्न"},"4":{"en":"Padma Bhushan","hi":"पद्म भूषण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Padma Vibhushan</b><br>Former Chief Justice of India <b>Jagdish Singh Khehar</b> was conferred the <b><u>Padma Vibhushan</u></b> in the <b>Padma Awards 2025</b> for public affairs.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• J.S. Khehar was the <b>44<sup>th</sup> CJI</b> and the first <b>Sikh</b> CJI (2017).<br>• He headed the bench in the <b>Triple Talaq</b> case and the <b>Right to Privacy</b> (Puttaswamy) judgment.<br>• Padma Vibhushan is India's <b>second-highest civilian award</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पद्म विभूषण</b><br>भारत के पूर्व मुख्य न्यायाधीश <b>जगदीश सिंह खेहर</b> को <b>पद्म पुरस्कार 2025</b> में सार्वजनिक मामलों के लिए <b><u>पद्म विभूषण</u></b> प्रदान किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• जे.एस. खेहर <b>44वें मुख्य न्यायाधीश</b> और पहले <b>सिख</b> मुख्य न्यायाधीश (2017) थे।<br>• उन्होंने <b>तीन तलाक</b> मामले और <b>निजता के अधिकार</b> (पुट्टास्वामी) निर्णय की पीठ का नेतृत्व किया।<br>• पद्म विभूषण भारत का <b>दूसरा सर्वोच्च नागरिक सम्मान</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000073224","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Census","question":{"en":"As per Census of India 2011, what is the <b>correct</b> distribution of male and female workers in the Primary sector? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत की जनगणना 2011 के अनुसार प्राथमिक क्षेत्र में पुरुष और महिला श्रमिकों का <b>सही</b> वितरण क्या है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Male – 15,66,43,220; Female – 4,37,41,311","hi":"पुरुष – 15,66,43,220; महिला – 4,37,41,311"},"2":{"en":"Male – 16,54,47,075; Female – 9,75,75,398","hi":"पुरुष – 16,54,47,075; महिला – 9,75,75,398"},"3":{"en":"Male – 16,54,47,075; Female – 4,37,41,311","hi":"पुरुष – 16,54,47,075; महिला – 4,37,41,311"},"4":{"en":"Male – 15,66,43,220; Female – 9,75,75,398","hi":"पुरुष – 15,66,43,220; महिला – 9,75,75,398"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Male – 16,54,47,075; Female – 9,75,75,398</b><br>As per the Census 2011 table in NCERT, primary sector workers were <b>Male – 16,54,47,075</b> and <b>Female – 9,75,75,398</b>, i.e., <b><u>option 2</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The primary sector employs the <b>largest share of female workers</b> in India.<br>• Tertiary sector (2011): Male – 15,66,43,220; Female – 4,37,41,311.<br>• Female work participation rate (2011): about <b>25.5%</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पुरुष – 16,54,47,075; महिला – 9,75,75,398</b><br>NCERT की जनगणना 2011 तालिका के अनुसार प्राथमिक क्षेत्र के श्रमिक <b>पुरुष – 16,54,47,075</b> और <b>महिला – 9,75,75,398</b> थे, अर्थात् <b><u>विकल्प 2</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत में <b>महिला श्रमिकों का सबसे बड़ा हिस्सा</b> प्राथमिक क्षेत्र में है।<br>• तृतीयक क्षेत्र (2011): पुरुष – 15,66,43,220; महिला – 4,37,41,311।<br>• महिला कार्य सहभागिता दर (2011): लगभग <b>25.5%</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000073225","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements regarding Indo-Islamic architecture:<br>1. Rubble masonry walls were commonly used in the construction of these buildings.<br>2. Mandu is a prominent example of Provincial Style architecture.<br>Which of the statements given above is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"हिंद-इस्लामी स्थापत्य के संबंध में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1. इन इमारतों के निर्माण में सामान्यतः मलबा चिनाई (रबल मेसनरी) की दीवारें प्रयुक्त हुईं।<br>2. मांडू प्रांतीय शैली स्थापत्य का प्रमुख उदाहरण है।<br>ऊपर दिए गए कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न तो 1 और न ही 2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Both 1 and 2</b><br>Indo-Islamic buildings commonly had thick <b>rubble masonry walls</b> covered with plaster or stone veneer, and <b>Mandu</b> (Malwa) is a fine example of the <b>Provincial style</b>. Both are correct: <b><u>Both 1 and 2</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Mandu monuments: <b>Jahaz Mahal, Hindola Mahal, Rani Roopmati's Pavilion, Jami Masjid</b>.<br>• Lime mortar (<b>chuna</b>) was widely used as cementing material.<br>• Mandu was the capital of the <b>Malwa Sultanate</b> (Baz Bahadur).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1 और 2 दोनों</b><br>हिंद-इस्लामी इमारतों में सामान्यतः प्लास्टर या पत्थर की परत से ढकी मोटी <b>मलबा चिनाई की दीवारें</b> होती थीं, और <b>मांडू</b> (मालवा) <b>प्रांतीय शैली</b> का उत्कृष्ट उदाहरण है। दोनों सही हैं: <b><u>1 और 2 दोनों</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मांडू के स्मारक: <b>जहाज़ महल, हिंडोला महल, रानी रूपमती मंडप, जामी मस्जिद</b>।<br>• जोड़ने वाली सामग्री के रूप में चूना-गारा (<b>चूना</b>) व्यापक रूप से प्रयुक्त हुआ।<br>• मांडू <b>मालवा सल्तनत</b> (बाज़ बहादुर) की राजधानी थी।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000073226","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"Which spacecraft platform serves as the base structure for the NISAR satellite? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"NISAR उपग्रह के आधार ढाँचे के रूप में कौन-सा अंतरिक्ष यान प्लेटफ़ॉर्म कार्य करता है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"I-1K spacecraft bus","hi":"I-1K स्पेसक्राफ्ट बस"},"2":{"en":"I-2K spacecraft bus","hi":"I-2K स्पेसक्राफ्ट बस"},"3":{"en":"I-3K spacecraft bus","hi":"I-3K स्पेसक्राफ्ट बस"},"4":{"en":"I-6K spacecraft bus","hi":"I-6K स्पेसक्राफ्ट बस"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – I-3K spacecraft bus</b><br>NISAR is built on ISRO's <b><u>I-3K spacecraft bus</u></b>, which provides power, attitude control and structure for the radar payloads; the satellite weighs about <b>2,392 kg</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• NISAR was launched on <b>30 July 2025</b> by <b>GSLV-F16</b> into a sun-synchronous orbit.<br>• Its <b>12 m</b> unfurlable mesh reflector antenna was provided by NASA.<br>• The I-3K bus is used for <b>3-tonne class</b> satellites like INSAT/GSAT.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – I-3K स्पेसक्राफ्ट बस</b><br>NISAR ISRO की <b><u>I-3K स्पेसक्राफ्ट बस</u></b> पर बना है, जो रडार पेलोड के लिए शक्ति, अभिवृत्ति नियंत्रण और संरचना देती है; उपग्रह का भार लगभग <b>2,392 kg</b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• NISAR <b>30 जुलाई 2025</b> को <b>GSLV-F16</b> से सूर्य-तुल्यकालिक कक्षा में प्रक्षेपित हुआ।<br>• इसका <b>12 m</b> का खुलने वाला मेश परावर्तक एंटीना NASA ने दिया।<br>• I-3K बस <b>3-टन श्रेणी</b> के उपग्रहों जैसे INSAT/GSAT में प्रयुक्त होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000073227","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Banking","question":{"en":"Which committee was appointed in 1991 to recommend reforms in India's banking and financial sector? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत के बैंकिंग और वित्तीय क्षेत्र में सुधारों की सिफारिश के लिए 1991 में कौन-सी समिति नियुक्त की गई? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Chelliah Committee","hi":"चेलैया समिति"},"2":{"en":"Rangrajan Committee","hi":"रंगराजन समिति"},"3":{"en":"Malhotra Committee","hi":"मल्होत्रा समिति"},"4":{"en":"Narasimham Committee","hi":"नरसिम्हम समिति"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Narasimham Committee</b><br>The <b><u>Narasimham Committee (1991)</u></b>, headed by <b>M. Narasimham</b>, recommended reforms in the financial system – reducing SLR and CRR, entry of private banks and autonomy to banks.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The second Narasimham Committee (1998) dealt with <b>banking sector reforms</b>.<br>• <b>Chelliah Committee</b> – tax reforms; <b>Malhotra Committee (1993)</b> – insurance.<br>• <b>Rangarajan Committee</b> – disinvestment (1993) and poverty estimation (2014).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – नरसिम्हम समिति</b><br><b>एम. नरसिम्हम</b> की अध्यक्षता में <b><u>नरसिम्हम समिति (1991)</u></b> ने वित्तीय प्रणाली में सुधारों की सिफारिश की – SLR और CRR घटाना, निजी बैंकों का प्रवेश और बैंकों को स्वायत्तता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• दूसरी नरसिम्हम समिति (1998) <b>बैंकिंग क्षेत्र सुधारों</b> से संबंधित थी।<br>• <b>चेलैया समिति</b> – कर सुधार; <b>मल्होत्रा समिति (1993)</b> – बीमा।<br>• <b>रंगराजन समिति</b> – विनिवेश (1993) और गरीबी आकलन (2014)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000073228","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"Under India’s National Air Quality Index framework, data for at least how many pollutants are required to calculate the Air Quality Index? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत के राष्ट्रीय वायु गुणवत्ता सूचकांक ढाँचे के तहत वायु गुणवत्ता सूचकांक की गणना के लिए कम से कम कितने प्रदूषकों का डेटा आवश्यक है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Two pollutants","hi":"दो प्रदूषक"},"2":{"en":"Three pollutants","hi":"तीन प्रदूषक"},"3":{"en":"Five pollutants","hi":"पाँच प्रदूषक"},"4":{"en":"Seven pollutants","hi":"सात प्रदूषक"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Three pollutants</b><br>The AQI is calculated if data for at least <b><u>three pollutants</u></b> is available, one of which must be <b>PM2.5 or PM10</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India's National AQI was launched in <b>2014</b> by <b>CPCB</b> under the Swachh Bharat Abhiyan.<br>• It covers <b>8 pollutants</b>: PM10, PM2.5, NO₂, SO₂, CO, O₃, NH₃, Pb.<br>• The overall AQI is the <b>highest sub-index</b> among the pollutants.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – तीन प्रदूषक</b><br>AQI की गणना तभी होती है जब कम से कम <b><u>तीन प्रदूषकों</u></b> का डेटा उपलब्ध हो, जिनमें से एक <b>PM2.5 या PM10</b> होना चाहिए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत का राष्ट्रीय AQI <b>2014</b> में स्वच्छ भारत अभियान के तहत <b>CPCB</b> ने शुरू किया।<br>• इसमें <b>8 प्रदूषक</b>: PM10, PM2.5, NO₂, SO₂, CO, O₃, NH₃, Pb।<br>• समग्र AQI प्रदूषकों में <b>सबसे अधिक उप-सूचकांक</b> होता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000073229","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Advent of Europeans","question":{"en":"Whose combined forces did Major Hector Munro defeat in the Battle of Buxar? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"बक्सर के युद्ध में मेजर हेक्टर मुनरो ने किसकी संयुक्त सेनाओं को पराजित किया? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mir Jafar, Shuja-ud-Daula, and Shah Alam II","hi":"मीर जाफ़र, शुजाउद्दौला और शाह आलम द्वितीय"},"2":{"en":"Mir Qasim, Shuja-ud-Daula, and Shah Alam II","hi":"मीर क़ासिम, शुजाउद्दौला और शाह आलम द्वितीय"},"3":{"en":"Mir Qasim, Najm-ud-Daula, and the Nizam","hi":"मीर क़ासिम, नज्मुद्दौला और निज़ाम"},"4":{"en":"Siraj-ud-Daula, Mir Jafar, and the Marathas","hi":"सिराजुद्दौला, मीर जाफ़र और मराठा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Mir Qasim, Shuja-ud-Daula, and Shah Alam II</b><br>In the <b>Battle of Buxar (22 October 1764)</b>, <b>Hector Munro</b> defeated the combined armies of <b><u>Mir Qasim (Bengal), Shuja-ud-Daula (Awadh) and Mughal emperor Shah Alam II</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It led to the <b>Treaty of Allahabad (1765)</b>, giving the Company the <b>Diwani</b> of Bengal, Bihar and Odisha.<br>• Buxar is considered more decisive than <b>Plassey (1757)</b>.<br>• Robert Clive introduced <b>Dual Government</b> in Bengal (1765–72).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मीर क़ासिम, शुजाउद्दौला और शाह आलम द्वितीय</b><br><b>बक्सर के युद्ध (22 अक्टूबर 1764)</b> में <b>हेक्टर मुनरो</b> ने <b><u>मीर क़ासिम (बंगाल), शुजाउद्दौला (अवध) और मुग़ल सम्राट शाह आलम द्वितीय</u></b> की संयुक्त सेनाओं को हराया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसके बाद <b>इलाहाबाद की संधि (1765)</b> हुई, जिससे कंपनी को बंगाल, बिहार और ओडिशा की <b>दीवानी</b> मिली।<br>• बक्सर को <b>प्लासी (1757)</b> से अधिक निर्णायक माना जाता है।<br>• रॉबर्ट क्लाइव ने बंगाल में <b>द्वैध शासन</b> (1765–72) शुरू किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000073230","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Nutrients","question":{"en":"A student burns 150 calories by cycling for 30 minutes. If the student continues cycling at the same rate, how many calories will be burned in 2 hours? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक छात्र 30 मिनट साइकिल चलाकर 150 कैलोरी जलाता है। यदि छात्र उसी दर से साइकिल चलाता रहे, तो 2 घंटे में कितनी कैलोरी जलेंगी? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"600"},"2":{"en":"450"},"3":{"en":"500"},"4":{"en":"900"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 600</b><br>Rate = 150 calories per 30 min = 5 calories per minute<br>2 hours = 120 minutes ⇒ 120 × 5 = <b><u>600 calories</u></b><br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• 1 food calorie (kcal) = <b>4.184 kJ</b>.<br>• Carbohydrates and proteins give about <b>4 kcal/g</b>; fats about <b>9 kcal/g</b>.<br>• Energy in food is released by <b>cellular respiration</b> in mitochondria.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – 600</b><br>दर = 150 कैलोरी प्रति 30 मिनट = 5 कैलोरी प्रति मिनट<br>2 घंटे = 120 मिनट ⇒ 120 × 5 = <b><u>600 कैलोरी</u></b><br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 1 खाद्य कैलोरी (kcal) = <b>4.184 kJ</b>।<br>• कार्बोहाइड्रेट और प्रोटीन लगभग <b>4 kcal/g</b>; वसा लगभग <b>9 kcal/g</b> ऊर्जा देते हैं।<br>• भोजन की ऊर्जा माइटोकॉन्ड्रिया में <b>कोशिकीय श्वसन</b> से मुक्त होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000073231","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A sphere of radius 'R' has a surface area equal to the curved surface area of a hemisphere with radius 'r'. Find the ratio of \\(\\frac{R}{r}\\). [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"'R' त्रिज्या वाले एक गोले का पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल 'r' त्रिज्या वाले अर्धगोले के वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल के बराबर है। \\(\\frac{R}{r}\\) का अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(4\\pi R^2 = 2\\pi r^2\\)<br>\\(\\frac{R^2}{r^2} = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{R}{r} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(4\\pi R^2 = 2\\pi r^2\\)<br>\\(\\frac{R^2}{r^2} = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{R}{r} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000073232","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"If the area of a triangle is 10√3 cm² and two of its sides are 5 cm and 8 cm, what is the included angle? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि एक त्रिभुज का क्षेत्रफल 10√3 cm² है और उसकी दो भुजाएँ 5 cm तथा 8 cm हैं, तो उनके बीच का कोण क्या है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30°"},"2":{"en":"45°"},"3":{"en":"60°"},"4":{"en":"90°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Area \\(= \\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{2}(5)(8)\\sin C = 10\\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow \\sin C = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)<br>\\(C = \\boxed{60°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 60°.</b>","hi":"क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{2}(5)(8)\\sin C = 10\\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow \\sin C = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)<br>\\(C = \\boxed{60°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 60° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000073233","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two regular polygons have (n − 1) and (n + 2) sides respectively. If the difference in their exterior angles is 6°, find the value of n. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दो सम बहुभुजों में क्रमशः (n − 1) और (n + 2) भुजाएँ हैं। यदि उनके बहिष्कोणों का अंतर 6° है, तो n का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15"},"2":{"en":"16"},"3":{"en":"14"},"4":{"en":"13"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{360}{n-1} - \\frac{360}{n+2} = 6\\)<br>\\(\\frac{3}{n-1} = \\frac{1}{20} \\Rightarrow n - 1 = 60\\)... simplifying gives \\(n = 13\\)<br>\\(n = \\boxed{13}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 13.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{360}{n-1} - \\frac{360}{n+2} = 6\\)<br>सरल करने पर \\(n = 13\\)<br>\\(n = \\boxed{13}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 13 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000073234","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If cosθ = 4/5, find tan²θ + sec²θ. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि cosθ = 4/5 है, तो tan²θ + sec²θ ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"17/8"},"3":{"en":"17/4"},"4":{"en":"5"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sec\\theta = \\frac{5}{4}\\), \\(\\tan^2\\theta = \\frac{25}{16} - 1 = \\frac{9}{16}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{9}{16} + \\frac{25}{16} = \\frac{34}{16}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{17}{8}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 17/8.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sec\\theta = \\frac{5}{4}\\), \\(\\tan^2\\theta = \\frac{25}{16} - 1 = \\frac{9}{16}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{9}{16} + \\frac{25}{16} = \\frac{34}{16}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{17}{8}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 17/8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000073235","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Examine the frequency polygon on student performance in a Math test between Section A and Section B, to answer the following question.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/01980b71-d38c-71ef-bf20-b16070f3803e_EN.jpg?edu=639294374004035978\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>What is the modal class for Section B? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"गणित की परीक्षा में सेक्शन A और सेक्शन B के छात्र प्रदर्शन पर आवृत्ति बहुभुज देखिए और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/01980b71-d38c-71ef-bf20-b16070f3803e_HI.jpg?edu=639294374137393735\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>सेक्शन B के लिए बहुलक वर्ग कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"21–40"},"2":{"en":"41–60"},"3":{"en":"61–80"},"4":{"en":"81–100"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Section B (dashed): 0, 5, 10, 20, 10<br>Highest frequency 20 at 61–80<br>\\(\\boxed{61-80}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 61–80.</b>","hi":"सेक्शन B (बिंदुकित): 0, 5, 10, 20, 10<br>सर्वाधिक आवृत्ति 20, वर्ग 61–80 में<br>\\(\\boxed{61-80}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 61–80 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/01980b71-d38c-71ef-bf20-b16070f3803e_EN.jpg?edu=639294374004035978","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/01980b71-d38c-71ef-bf20-b16070f3803e_HI.jpg?edu=639294374137393735"]}},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000073236","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"Examine the bar graph below to answer the following question.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/01981156-e60a-7a23-bf60-cab8a652d3c7_EN.jpg?edu=639294374004132173\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If rainfall in Kolkata increases by 20% and rainfall in Jaipur decreases by 25%, what will be the simplified ratio of highest to lowest rainfall among all cities? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"नीचे दिया गया बार ग्राफ देखिए और प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/01981156-e60a-7a23-bf60-cab8a652d3c7_HI.jpg?edu=639294374137465323\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि कोलकाता में वर्षा 20% बढ़ जाए और जयपुर में वर्षा 25% घट जाए, तो सभी शहरों में सर्वाधिक और न्यूनतम वर्षा का सरलीकृत अनुपात क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18:5"},"2":{"en":"17:4"},"3":{"en":"16:5"},"4":{"en":"15:4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Rainfall: Delhi 90, Mumbai 315, Kolkata 270, Chennai 185, Jaipur 120 (mm)<br>New Kolkata \\(= 324\\), new Jaipur \\(= 90\\); lowest is Delhi 90<br>Highest 324, lowest 90 \\(\\Rightarrow 324 : 90 = \\boxed{18:5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 18:5.</b>","hi":"वर्षा: दिल्ली 90, मुंबई 315, कोलकाता 270, चेन्नई 185, जयपुर 120 (mm)<br>नई कोलकाता \\(= 324\\), नया जयपुर \\(= 90\\); न्यूनतम दिल्ली 90<br>सर्वाधिक 324, न्यूनतम 90 \\(\\Rightarrow 324 : 90 = \\boxed{18:5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 18:5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/01981156-e60a-7a23-bf60-cab8a652d3c7_EN.jpg?edu=639294374004132173","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/01981156-e60a-7a23-bf60-cab8a652d3c7_HI.jpg?edu=639294374137465323"]}},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000073237","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"Examine the bar graph below to answer the following question.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0198119c-4618-7247-ad39-d2c386867e7b_EN.jpg?edu=639294374004242168\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Which vehicle type has the highest diesel-to-petrol consumption ratio, and what is that ratio? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"नीचे दिया गया बार ग्राफ देखिए और प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0198119c-4618-7247-ad39-d2c386867e7b_HI.jpg?edu=639294374137552031\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>किस वाहन प्रकार का डीज़ल-से-पेट्रोल खपत अनुपात सर्वाधिक है, और वह अनुपात क्या है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bus – 9:1","hi":"बस – 9:1"},"2":{"en":"Truck – 20:3","hi":"ट्रक – 20:3"},"3":{"en":"Car – 4:3","hi":"कार – 4:3"},"4":{"en":"Van – 2:1","hi":"वैन – 2:1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Bars: Car 45/60, Bus 10/90, Bike 50/5, Truck 18/100, Van 30/60<br>Ratios: 1.33, 9, 0.1, 5.56, 2<br>Highest \\(= \\boxed{\\text{Bus} - 9:1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Bus – 9:1.</b>","hi":"बार: कार 45/60, बस 10/90, बाइक 50/5, ट्रक 18/100, वैन 30/60<br>अनुपात: 1.33, 9, 0.1, 5.56, 2<br>सर्वाधिक \\(= \\boxed{\\text{बस} - 9:1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): बस – 9:1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0198119c-4618-7247-ad39-d2c386867e7b_EN.jpg?edu=639294374004242168","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0198119c-4618-7247-ad39-d2c386867e7b_HI.jpg?edu=639294374137552031"]}},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000073238","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"Study the pie chart carefully. It shows how a household allocates its monthly budget across different categories. Then answer the following questions.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0198121b-c67d-7991-8c0d-04b13e814912_EN.jpg?edu=639294374004370862\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If the total monthly income is $4,000, how much money is spent on Groceries? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पाई चार्ट को ध्यान से पढ़िए। यह दर्शाता है कि एक परिवार अपना मासिक बजट विभिन्न श्रेणियों में कैसे बाँटता है। फिर निम्नलिखित प्रश्नों का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0198121b-c67d-7991-8c0d-04b13e814912_HI.jpg?edu=639294374137646087\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि कुल मासिक आय $4,000 है, तो किराने पर कितना खर्च होता है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"$700"},"2":{"en":"$800"},"3":{"en":"$900"},"4":{"en":"$1,000"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Groceries \\(= 20\\%\\) of the budget<br>\\(= 0.20 \\times 4000\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{800}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): $800.</b>","hi":"किराना \\(= \\) बजट का 20%<br>\\(= 0.20 \\times 4000\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{800}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): $800 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/0198121b-c67d-7991-8c0d-04b13e814912_EN.jpg?edu=639294374004370862","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/0198121b-c67d-7991-8c0d-04b13e814912_HI.jpg?edu=639294374137646087"]}},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000073239","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Examine the histogram showing how many employees fall within various salary ranges (in thousands of dollars). Use this data to answer the questions below.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/01981222-bbed-725f-85a7-83b30d6e13b2_EN.jpg?edu=639294374004504682\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Based on the histogram, which salary range has the highest number of employees? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"विभिन्न वेतन श्रेणियों (हज़ार डॉलर में) में कितने कर्मचारी हैं, यह दर्शाने वाला आयतचित्र देखिए। इस डेटा का उपयोग करके नीचे दिए प्रश्नों का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/01981222-bbed-725f-85a7-83b30d6e13b2_HI.jpg?edu=639294374137752533\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>आयतचित्र के आधार पर किस वेतन श्रेणी में सर्वाधिक कर्मचारी हैं? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20–30 thousand","hi":"20–30 हज़ार"},"2":{"en":"30–40 thousand","hi":"30–40 हज़ार"},"3":{"en":"40–50 thousand","hi":"40–50 हज़ार"},"4":{"en":"60–70 thousand","hi":"60–70 हज़ार"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Frequencies: 100, 200, 290, 400, 550, 450, 300, 250, 100, 100<br>Highest bar (550) is for 40–50<br>\\(\\boxed{40-50\\ \\text{thousand}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 40–50 thousand.</b>","hi":"आवृत्तियाँ: 100, 200, 290, 400, 550, 450, 300, 250, 100, 100<br>सबसे ऊँचा बार (550), वर्ग 40–50<br>\\(\\boxed{40-50\\ \\text{हज़ार}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 40–50 हज़ार है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/01981222-bbed-725f-85a7-83b30d6e13b2_EN.jpg?edu=639294374004504682","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/01981222-bbed-725f-85a7-83b30d6e13b2_HI.jpg?edu=639294374137752533"]}},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000073240","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\frac{(5.4)^3 - 1}{(5.4)^2 + 6.4}\\). [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"\\(\\frac{(5.4)^3 - 1}{(5.4)^2 + 6.4}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3.8"},"2":{"en":"4.4"},"3":{"en":"7.6"},"4":{"en":"5.8"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{a^3 - 1}{a^2 + a + 1} = a - 1\\) with \\(a = 5.4\\)<br>\\(= 5.4 - 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{4.4}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4.4.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{a^3 - 1}{a^2 + a + 1} = a - 1\\), जहाँ \\(a = 5.4\\)<br>\\(= 5.4 - 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{4.4}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4.4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000073241","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"The value of \\(\\frac{(2.4)^3 - (0.4)^3}{(2.4)^2 + 0.96 + (0.4)^2}\\) expressed as a fraction in simplest form is: [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"\\(\\frac{(2.4)^3 - (0.4)^3}{(2.4)^2 + 0.96 + (0.4)^2}\\) का मान सरलतम भिन्न के रूप में है: [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{6}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2}{1}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\) with \\(a = 2.4\\), \\(b = 0.4\\) (\\(ab = 0.96\\))<br>\\(= 2.4 - 0.4 = 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{2}{1}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\frac{2}{1}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\), जहाँ \\(a = 2.4\\), \\(b = 0.4\\) (\\(ab = 0.96\\))<br>\\(= 2.4 - 0.4 = 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{2}{1}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\frac{2}{1}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000073242","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"Find the third proportional of \\((\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{3})\\) and \\(4\\sqrt{6}\\). [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"\\((\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{3})\\) और \\(4\\sqrt{6}\\) का तृतीय अनुपाती ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(14(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(42(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2})\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(96(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(28(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2})\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Third proportional \\(= \\frac{b^2}{a} = \\frac{96}{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>Rationalise: \\(\\frac{96(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})}{3 - 2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{96(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(96(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})\\).</b>","hi":"तृतीय अनुपाती \\(= \\frac{b^2}{a} = \\frac{96}{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>परिमेयकरण: \\(\\frac{96(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})}{3 - 2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{96(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(96(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000073243","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"The ratio between the tens digit and the units digit of a two-digit number is 2:1. If the original number is 18 more than the number obtained by reversing the digits, find the original number. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दो अंकों की एक संख्या के दहाई अंक और इकाई अंक का अनुपात 2:1 है। यदि मूल संख्या अंकों को उलटने से प्राप्त संख्या से 18 अधिक है, तो मूल संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"28"},"2":{"en":"42"},"3":{"en":"54"},"4":{"en":"35"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let digits be \\(2x\\) (tens) and \\(x\\) (units)<br>\\((20x + x) - (10x + 2x) = 18 \\Rightarrow 9x = 18 \\Rightarrow x = 2\\)<br>Number \\(= \\boxed{42}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 42.</b>","hi":"अंक \\(2x\\) (दहाई) और \\(x\\) (इकाई) मानिए<br>\\((20x + x) - (10x + 2x) = 18 \\Rightarrow 9x = 18 \\Rightarrow x = 2\\)<br>संख्या \\(= \\boxed{42}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 42 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000073244","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In △ZWR, the bisector of ∠R meets side ZW at S, ZR = 10 cm, RW = 14 cm and ZW = 12 cm. What is the length of SW? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"△ZWR में, ∠R का समद्विभाजक भुजा ZW को S पर मिलता है, ZR = 10 cm, RW = 14 cm और ZW = 12 cm है। SW की लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 cm"},"2":{"en":"7 cm"},"3":{"en":"11 cm"},"4":{"en":"17 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Angle bisector theorem: \\(\\frac{ZS}{SW} = \\frac{ZR}{RW} = \\frac{10}{14} = \\frac{5}{7}\\)<br>\\(SW = \\frac{7}{12} \\times 12\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{7\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 7 cm.</b>","hi":"कोण समद्विभाजक प्रमेय: \\(\\frac{ZS}{SW} = \\frac{ZR}{RW} = \\frac{10}{14} = \\frac{5}{7}\\)<br>\\(SW = \\frac{7}{12} \\times 12\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{7\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 7 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000073245","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper marks his goods at 30% above the cost price. If the cost price increases by 15% and he increases the selling price by 10%, what is his new approximate profit percentage? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक दुकानदार अपने माल पर क्रय मूल्य से 30% अधिक अंकन करता है। यदि क्रय मूल्य 15% बढ़ जाए और वह विक्रय मूल्य 10% बढ़ा दे, तो उसका नया अनुमानित लाभ प्रतिशत क्या है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"17.35%"},"2":{"en":"24.35%"},"3":{"en":"12.35%"},"4":{"en":"28.35%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let CP \\(= 100\\), SP \\(= 130\\)<br>New CP \\(= 115\\), new SP \\(= 143\\)<br>Profit \\(= \\frac{143 - 115}{115} \\times 100 = \\boxed{24.35\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 24.35%.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए क्रय मूल्य \\(= 100\\), विक्रय मूल्य \\(= 130\\)<br>नया क्रय मूल्य \\(= 115\\), नया विक्रय मूल्य \\(= 143\\)<br>लाभ \\(= \\frac{143 - 115}{115} \\times 100 = \\boxed{24.35\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 24.35% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000073246","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A chord subtends 130° at the centre. What is the sum of angles subtended by it at a point on the major arc and minor arc? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक जीवा केंद्र पर 130° का कोण बनाती है। दीर्घ चाप और लघु चाप पर स्थित बिंदुओं पर इसके द्वारा बनाए गए कोणों का योग क्या है? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"120°"},"2":{"en":"180°"},"3":{"en":"200°"},"4":{"en":"240°"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Angle at a point on the major arc \\(= \\frac{130°}{2} = 65°\\)<br>Angle on the minor arc \\(= 180° - 65° = 115°\\)<br>Sum \\(= \\boxed{180°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 180°.</b>","hi":"दीर्घ चाप के बिंदु पर कोण \\(= \\frac{130°}{2} = 65°\\)<br>लघु चाप पर कोण \\(= 180° - 65° = 115°\\)<br>योग \\(= \\boxed{180°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 180° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000073247","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The area of a trapezium is 475 cm², and its height is 19 cm. If the parallel sides are in the ratio 2:3, find the length of the longer parallel side. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक समलंब का क्षेत्रफल 475 cm² और ऊँचाई 19 cm है। यदि समांतर भुजाएँ 2:3 के अनुपात में हैं, तो बड़ी समांतर भुजा की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20 cm"},"2":{"en":"30 cm"},"3":{"en":"35 cm"},"4":{"en":"25 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}(2x + 3x) \\times 19 = 475\\)<br>\\(5x = 50 \\Rightarrow x = 10\\)<br>Longer side \\(= 3x = \\boxed{30\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 30 cm.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}(2x + 3x) \\times 19 = 475\\)<br>\\(5x = 50 \\Rightarrow x = 10\\)<br>बड़ी भुजा \\(= 3x = \\boxed{30\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 30 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000073248","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In a circle with center O, PQ is the diameter and RS is a chord such that PQRS is a trapezium. If ∠QPR = 30°, find the measure of ∠RPS. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"केंद्र O वाले एक वृत्त में, PQ व्यास है और RS एक जीवा है जिससे PQRS एक समलंब बनता है। यदि ∠QPR = 30° है, तो ∠RPS का माप ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30°"},"2":{"en":"20°"},"3":{"en":"25°"},"4":{"en":"40°"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"PQRS is a cyclic trapezium with PQ ∥ RS, hence it is isosceles: PR = QS<br>\\(\\angle QPR = \\angle PQS = 30°\\) (alternate angles with PQ ∥ RS, and equal base angles)<br>Along the chord RS the angles are equal: \\(\\angle RPS = \\boxed{30°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 30°.</b>","hi":"PQRS एक चक्रीय समलंब है जिसमें PQ ∥ RS है, अतः यह समद्विबाहु है: PR = QS<br>\\(\\angle QPR = \\angle PQS = 30°\\)<br>जीवा RS पर बने कोण बराबर हैं: \\(\\angle RPS = \\boxed{30°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 30° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000073249","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In △ABC and △DEF, ∠A = 55°, AB = DE, AC = DF, ∠E = 85° and ∠F = 40°. By which property are △ABC and △DEF congruent? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"△ABC और △DEF में, ∠A = 55°, AB = DE, AC = DF, ∠E = 85° और ∠F = 40° है। △ABC और △DEF किस गुणधर्म से सर्वांगसम हैं? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RHS property","hi":"RHS गुणधर्म"},"2":{"en":"SSS property","hi":"SSS गुणधर्म"},"3":{"en":"SAS property","hi":"SAS गुणधर्म"},"4":{"en":"ASA property","hi":"ASA गुणधर्म"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Two sides and the included angle match: AB = DE, AC = DF and \\(\\angle A = \\angle D\\) (\\(180° - 85° - 40° = 55°\\) in △DEF)<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{SAS property}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): SAS property.</b>","hi":"दो भुजाएँ और उनके बीच का कोण मेल खाते हैं: AB = DE, AC = DF तथा \\(\\angle A = \\angle D\\) (△DEF में \\(180° - 85° - 40° = 55°\\))<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{SAS गुणधर्म}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): SAS गुणधर्म है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000073250","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two congruent circles, each having radius 12 cm, intersect in such a way that each circle passes through the centre of the other. Find the length of their common chord. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"12 cm त्रिज्या वाले दो सर्वांगसम वृत्त इस प्रकार प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं कि प्रत्येक वृत्त दूसरे के केंद्र से होकर जाता है। उनकी उभयनिष्ठ जीवा की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4 cm"},"2":{"en":"\\(6\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"},"3":{"en":"8 cm"},"4":{"en":"\\(12\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Centre distance \\(= 12\\) cm, so each centre is 6 cm from the common chord<br>Half chord \\(= \\sqrt{144 - 36} = \\sqrt{108} = 6\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>Chord \\(= \\boxed{12\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(12\\sqrt{3}\\) cm.</b>","hi":"केंद्रों की दूरी \\(= 12\\) cm, अतः प्रत्येक केंद्र उभयनिष्ठ जीवा से 6 cm दूर है<br>आधी जीवा \\(= \\sqrt{144 - 36} = \\sqrt{108} = 6\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>जीवा \\(= \\boxed{12\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(12\\sqrt{3}\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000073251","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A trader purchased 25 kg of tea at ₹240 per kg and another 15 kg at ₹300 per kg. After mixing both varieties, at what price per kg should the mixture be sold to earn a profit of 25%? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक व्यापारी ने 25 kg चाय ₹240 प्रति kg पर और 15 kg चाय ₹300 प्रति kg पर खरीदी। दोनों किस्में मिलाने के बाद 25% लाभ कमाने के लिए मिश्रण को प्रति kg किस मूल्य पर बेचना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹228.225 per kg","hi":"₹228.225 प्रति kg"},"2":{"en":"₹312.198 per kg","hi":"₹312.198 प्रति kg"},"3":{"en":"₹250.182 per kg","hi":"₹250.182 प्रति kg"},"4":{"en":"₹328.125 per kg","hi":"₹328.125 प्रति kg"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Total cost \\(= 25 \\times 240 + 15 \\times 300 = 6000 + 4500 = 10500\\)<br>Cost per kg \\(= \\frac{10500}{40} = 262.5\\)<br>Selling price \\(= 1.25 \\times 262.5 = \\boxed{328.125}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹328.125 per kg.</b>","hi":"कुल लागत \\(= 25 \\times 240 + 15 \\times 300 = 6000 + 4500 = 10500\\)<br>प्रति kg लागत \\(= \\frac{10500}{40} = 262.5\\)<br>विक्रय मूल्य \\(= 1.25 \\times 262.5 = \\boxed{328.125}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹328.125 प्रति kg है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000073252","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Three circles of radii 1 unit, 2 units, 3 units are mutually tangent externally. Find the distance between the centers of circles of radii 1 unit and 2 units. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"1 इकाई, 2 इकाइयाँ और 3 इकाइयाँ त्रिज्या वाले तीन वृत्त परस्पर बाह्य रूप से स्पर्श करते हैं। 1 इकाई और 2 इकाइयाँ त्रिज्या वाले वृत्तों के केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3 units","hi":"3 इकाई"},"2":{"en":"2 units","hi":"2 इकाई"},"3":{"en":"1 unit","hi":"1 इकाई"},"4":{"en":"4 units","hi":"4 इकाई"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"For externally tangent circles, centre distance \\(= r_1 + r_2\\)<br>\\(= 1 + 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3\\ \\text{units}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 3 units.</b>","hi":"बाह्य रूप से स्पर्श करने वाले वृत्तों के लिए केंद्रों की दूरी \\(= r_1 + r_2\\)<br>\\(= 1 + 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3\\ \\text{इकाई}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 3 इकाई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000073253","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The following pie-chart presents the percentage distribution of the population across five different regions. Study the pie-chart carefully and answer the question based on the provided data.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019e6daa-9ac9-7a1a-9281-4ddddb9d3702_EN.jpg?edu=639294374008056824\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If the population of all regions grows at an annual rate of 5%, except for Region D, which grows at 15% per annum, what will be the approximate percentage share of Region D in the total population after one year? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित पाई चार्ट पाँच अलग-अलग क्षेत्रों में जनसंख्या का प्रतिशत वितरण दर्शाता है। पाई चार्ट का ध्यान से अध्ययन कीजिए और दिए गए डेटा के आधार पर प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019e6daa-9ac9-7a1a-9281-4ddddb9d3702_HI.jpg?edu=639294374140390545\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि सभी क्षेत्रों की जनसंख्या 5% वार्षिक दर से बढ़ती है, सिवाय क्षेत्र D के जो 15% प्रतिवर्ष की दर से बढ़ता है, तो एक वर्ष बाद कुल जनसंख्या में क्षेत्र D का अनुमानित प्रतिशत हिस्सा क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18.5%"},"2":{"en":"19.4%"},"3":{"en":"22.8%"},"4":{"en":"24.6%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Shares: A 28, B 22, C 20, D 18, E 12; take total 100<br>After a year: others \\(\\times 1.05\\), D \\(\\times 1.15\\)<br>Total \\(= 82(1.05) + 18(1.15) = 86.1 + 20.7 = 106.8\\); D \\(= 20.7\\)<br>\\(\\frac{20.7}{106.8} \\times 100 \\approx \\boxed{19.4\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 19.4%.</b>","hi":"हिस्से: A 28, B 22, C 20, D 18, E 12; कुल 100 मानिए<br>एक वर्ष बाद: अन्य \\(\\times 1.05\\), D \\(\\times 1.15\\)<br>कुल \\(= 82(1.05) + 18(1.15) = 86.1 + 20.7 = 106.8\\); D \\(= 20.7\\)<br>\\(\\frac{20.7}{106.8} \\times 100 \\approx \\boxed{19.4\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 19.4% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/EN/019e6daa-9ac9-7a1a-9281-4ddddb9d3702_EN.jpg?edu=639294374008056824","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct9/qimg/3/HI/019e6daa-9ac9-7a1a-9281-4ddddb9d3702_HI.jpg?edu=639294374140390545"]}},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000073254","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A vertical pole of height H is situated at the center of a circular field. If the angle of elevation of the top of the pole from a point on the boundary of the field is 30°, and if the point moves x meters further from the pole, the angle of elevation becomes 15°. Find the height H of the pole. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"H ऊँचाई का एक ऊर्ध्वाधर खंभा एक वृत्ताकार मैदान के केंद्र में स्थित है। यदि मैदान की सीमा पर स्थित किसी बिंदु से खंभे के शीर्ष का उन्नयन कोण 30° है, और यदि वह बिंदु खंभे से x मीटर और दूर चला जाए तो उन्नयन कोण 15° हो जाता है। खंभे की ऊँचाई H ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{x}{2}\\) m"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{x}{4}\\) m"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) m"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{6}\\) m"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Radius of field \\(= H\\cot 30° = H\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{H}{H\\sqrt{3} + x} = \\tan 15° = 2 - \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>Solving: \\(H(2 - \\sqrt{3})\\sqrt{3} + x(2 - \\sqrt{3}) = H \\Rightarrow H = \\boxed{\\frac{x}{2}\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{x}{2}\\) m.</b>","hi":"मैदान की त्रिज्या \\(= H\\cot 30° = H\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{H}{H\\sqrt{3} + x} = \\tan 15° = 2 - \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>हल करने पर \\(H(2 - \\sqrt{3})\\sqrt{3} + x(2 - \\sqrt{3}) = H \\Rightarrow H = \\boxed{\\frac{x}{2}\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{x}{2}\\) m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000073255","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"The population of a tech hub increases by \\(16\\frac{2}{3}\\%\\) in the first year, decreases by \\(12\\frac{1}{2}\\%\\) in the second year, and increases by \\(14\\frac{2}{7}\\%\\) in the third year. If the population at the end of the third year is 2,80,000, what was the initial population before the first year? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक टेक हब की जनसंख्या पहले वर्ष में \\(16\\frac{2}{3}\\%\\) बढ़ती है, दूसरे वर्ष में \\(12\\frac{1}{2}\\%\\) घटती है और तीसरे वर्ष में \\(14\\frac{2}{7}\\%\\) बढ़ती है। यदि तीसरे वर्ष के अंत में जनसंख्या 2,80,000 है, तो पहले वर्ष से पहले प्रारंभिक जनसंख्या क्या थी? [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2,25,000"},"2":{"en":"2,10,000"},"3":{"en":"2,50,000"},"4":{"en":"2,40,000"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Factors: \\(\\frac{7}{6}\\), \\(\\frac{7}{8}\\), \\(\\frac{8}{7}\\)<br>Product \\(= \\frac{7}{6} \\times \\frac{7}{8} \\times \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{7}{6}\\)<br>\\(P \\times \\frac{7}{6} = 280000 \\Rightarrow P = \\boxed{2{,}40{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2,40,000.</b>","hi":"गुणक: \\(\\frac{7}{6}\\), \\(\\frac{7}{8}\\), \\(\\frac{8}{7}\\)<br>गुणनफल \\(= \\frac{7}{6} \\times \\frac{7}{8} \\times \\frac{8}{7} = \\frac{7}{6}\\)<br>\\(P \\times \\frac{7}{6} = 280000 \\Rightarrow P = \\boxed{2{,}40{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 2,40,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000073256","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), and (4). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>Throughout history, the evolution of women's clothing has mirrored broader societal shifts, (1)___ values, technologies, and power structures. In ancient civilizations, garments often (2)___ not only status and wealth but also cultural affiliations, with fabrics and dyes reserved for the privileged classes. The Middle Ages introduced rigid dress codes; women's attire, elaborate and weighty, served as both an ornament and a restraint, subtly (3)___ entrenching gender hierarchies. Fast-forwarding to the 20th century, movements like suffrage and feminism (4)___ catalyzed seismic transformations in fashion, promoting practicality, autonomy, and self-expression. Even today, the politics of women's clothing (5)___ a battleground for debates on identity, freedom, and societal expectations.<br><br><br>Choose the correct tense/form (1) [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"reflecting"},"2":{"en":"reflected"},"3":{"en":"having reflected"},"4":{"en":"reflects"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A present participle adds an accompanying result or explanation.</b><br>“Reflecting values, technologies, and power structures” describes how clothing mirrors societal shifts.<br>“Reflected” would create an unsuitable finite or passive construction after the comma.<br>“Having reflected” emphasizes prior completion unnecessarily; “reflects” would create a second unconnected finite verb.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): reflecting.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000073257","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), and (4). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>Throughout history, the evolution of women's clothing has mirrored broader societal shifts, (1)___ values, technologies, and power structures. In ancient civilizations, garments often (2)___ not only status and wealth but also cultural affiliations, with fabrics and dyes reserved for the privileged classes. The Middle Ages introduced rigid dress codes; women's attire, elaborate and weighty, served as both an ornament and a restraint, subtly (3)___ entrenching gender hierarchies. Fast-forwarding to the 20th century, movements like suffrage and feminism (4)___ catalyzed seismic transformations in fashion, promoting practicality, autonomy, and self-expression. Even today, the politics of women's clothing (5)___ a battleground for debates on identity, freedom, and societal expectations.<br><br><br>Tense carefully! (2) [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"signify"},"2":{"en":"has signified"},"3":{"en":"signifies"},"4":{"en":"signifying"}},"answer":"3","solution":{},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000073258","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), and (4). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>Throughout history, the evolution of women's clothing has mirrored broader societal shifts, (1)___ values, technologies, and power structures. In ancient civilizations, garments often (2)___ not only status and wealth but also cultural affiliations, with fabrics and dyes reserved for the privileged classes. The Middle Ages introduced rigid dress codes; women's attire, elaborate and weighty, served as both an ornament and a restraint, subtly (3)___ entrenching gender hierarchies. Fast-forwarding to the 20th century, movements like suffrage and feminism (4)___ catalyzed seismic transformations in fashion, promoting practicality, autonomy, and self-expression. Even today, the politics of women's clothing (5)___ a battleground for debates on identity, freedom, and societal expectations.<br><br><br>In this context, “entrenching” most nearly means: (3) [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Strengthening"},"2":{"en":"Questioning"},"3":{"en":"Obliterating"},"4":{"en":"Simplifying"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Entrenching (गहराई से स्थापित करना) = firmly establishing or strengthening.</b><br>Rigid dress codes strengthened existing gender hierarchies.<br><b>Questioning (प्रश्न करना)</b> = challenging<br><b>Obliterating (मिटा देना)</b> = destroying completely; <b>simplifying (सरल बनाना)</b> = making less complex<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Strengthening.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000073259","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), and (4). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>Throughout history, the evolution of women's clothing has mirrored broader societal shifts, (1)___ values, technologies, and power structures. In ancient civilizations, garments often (2)___ not only status and wealth but also cultural affiliations, with fabrics and dyes reserved for the privileged classes. The Middle Ages introduced rigid dress codes; women's attire, elaborate and weighty, served as both an ornament and a restraint, subtly (3)___ entrenching gender hierarchies. Fast-forwarding to the 20th century, movements like suffrage and feminism (4)___ catalyzed seismic transformations in fashion, promoting practicality, autonomy, and self-expression. Even today, the politics of women's clothing (5)___ a battleground for debates on identity, freedom, and societal expectations.<br><br><br>What does “catalyzed” most nearly mean here? (4) [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hindered"},"2":{"en":"Stimulated"},"3":{"en":"Disguised"},"4":{"en":"Delayed"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Catalyzed (उत्तेजित/गति दी) = triggered or accelerated a change.</b><br>“Stimulated” best describes how suffrage and feminism accelerated transformations in fashion.<br><b>Hindered (बाधा डाली)</b> = obstructed<br><b>Disguised (छिपाया)</b> = concealed; <b>delayed (विलंबित किया)</b> = made late<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Stimulated.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000073260","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), and (4). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>Throughout history, the evolution of women's clothing has mirrored broader societal shifts, (1)___ values, technologies, and power structures. In ancient civilizations, garments often (2)___ not only status and wealth but also cultural affiliations, with fabrics and dyes reserved for the privileged classes. The Middle Ages introduced rigid dress codes; women's attire, elaborate and weighty, served as both an ornament and a restraint, subtly (3)___ entrenching gender hierarchies. Fast-forwarding to the 20th century, movements like suffrage and feminism (4)___ catalyzed seismic transformations in fashion, promoting practicality, autonomy, and self-expression. Even today, the politics of women's clothing (5)___ a battleground for debates on identity, freedom, and societal expectations.<br><br><br>Choose the best tense form of the verb. (5) [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"remains"},"2":{"en":"has remained"},"3":{"en":"remain"},"4":{"en":"had remained"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Singular “the politics” takes a singular present verb.</b><br>“Even today” establishes the present time, so “remains” is correct.<br>“Has remained” unnecessarily emphasizes continuity from a past starting point.<br>“Remain” does not agree with the singular subject; “had remained” requires a past reference point.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): remains.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000073261","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the correct direct speech form of the following sentence.<br>She told him that he would play basketball. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She said to him, “You should play basketball.”"},"2":{"en":"She said to him, “You would play basketball.”"},"3":{"en":"She said to him, “You will play basketball.”"},"4":{"en":"She said to him, “He would play basketball.”"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Would” returns to “will,” and the reported third person returns to “you.”</b><br>The listener is “him,” so the direct address is “You will play basketball.”<br>A changes the modal to “should”; B retains “would.”<br>D retains third-person “he” and therefore does not address the listener.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): She said to him, “You will play basketball.”.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000073262","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Phrasal Verbs","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with an appropriate phrasal verb.<br>After initial hesitation, the entrepreneur finally ___ the risky investment. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"plumped for"},"2":{"en":"leaned over"},"3":{"en":"leaned over"},"4":{"en":"plunged out"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Plump for (चुनना) = choose something after careful thought or hesitation.</b><br>The entrepreneur finally chose the risky investment.<br><b>Lean over (झुकना)</b> = bend over something<br>“Plunged out” is not an idiomatic choice expression; it does not fit the sentence.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): plumped for.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000073263","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br>She completed the assignment quick to meet the deadline. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"quick"},"2":{"en":"deadline"},"3":{"en":"assignment"},"4":{"en":"completed"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Use an adverb to modify the verb “completed.”</b><br>“Quick” is an adjective, so the erroneous word is “quick.”<br>Correct sentence: “She completed the assignment <b>quickly</b> to meet the deadline.”<br>The other words are grammatically correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): quick.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000073264","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br>There is no point in discussing the new project with him as he always <b>pours cold water on</b> any ideas. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He strongly supports new ideas."},"2":{"en":"He discourages or criticizes new ideas."},"3":{"en":"He ignores new ideas completely."},"4":{"en":"He enthusiastically accepts new ideas."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Pour cold water on (उत्साह भंग करना) = discourage or criticize an idea.</b><br>Example: “The manager poured cold water on our proposal.”<br>Strong support and enthusiastic acceptance are the opposite.<br>Complete ignoring does not capture the active discouragement or criticism.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): He discourages or criticizes new ideas..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000073265","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>The enforcement of international human rights laws<br>P. to hold violators accountable for war crimes and genocide<br>Q. has faced obstacles due to political resistance,<br>R. despite the establishment of global courts and legal frameworks<br>S. and the complexities of diplomatic immunity in sovereign states [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SRQP"},"2":{"en":"QRSP"},"3":{"en":"PSQR"},"4":{"en":"RSQP"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QRSP</b><br>Q gives the main predicate and first obstacle: political resistance.<br>S adds the complexities of diplomatic immunity.<br>R supplies the contrast with global courts, and P states their purpose of holding violators accountable.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): QRSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000073266","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br>She didn’t realize that the clever salesman was <b>taking her for a ride</b>. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Giving her a lift in his car"},"2":{"en":"Cheating or deceiving her"},"3":{"en":"Taking her on an amusement park ride"},"4":{"en":"Offering her a business opportunity"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Take someone for a ride (ठगना) = cheat or deceive someone.</b><br>The clever salesman was misleading her, not literally driving her somewhere.<br>Example: “The customer was taken for a ride by the fraudulent seller.”<br>A lift, amusement ride and business offer do not convey deception.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Cheating or deceiving her.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000073267","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Improve the sentence by selecting the appropriate preposition from the following options.<br>The intricate designs of the ancient manuscript were hidden ___ the layers of dust and time, waiting to be rediscovered by modern scholars. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"over"},"2":{"en":"outside"},"3":{"en":"beneath"},"4":{"en":"on"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Beneath (नीचे) = under or covered by something.</b><br>The designs lay beneath layers of dust and time.<br>“Over” and “on” place the designs above the layers, reversing the image.<br>“Outside” means external to something and does not express concealment.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): beneath.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000073268","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence<br>He passed away the forms to the candidates. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"forms"},"2":{"en":"passed"},"3":{"en":"away"},"4":{"en":"candidates"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Pass out” means distribute; “pass away” means die.</b><br>The erroneous word is “away.”<br>Correct sentence: “He passed <b>out</b> the forms to the candidates.”<br>“Forms” and “candidates” are appropriate objects in this context.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): away.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000073269","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to fill in the blank.<br>I was practising the guitar ___. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"codes"},"2":{"en":"cords"},"3":{"en":"chords"},"4":{"en":"cards"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Chords (स्वर-संयोजन) = groups of musical notes played together.</b><br>Guitar practice involves chords.<br><b>Codes (संकेत)</b> = systems of rules or symbols<br><b>Cords (रस्सियाँ)</b> = strings or ropes; <b>cards (पत्ते)</b> = pieces of stiff paper<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): chords.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000073270","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correctly spelt word.<br>The ___ behavior of electrons challenged classical physics. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"anomaleous"},"2":{"en":"anomallous"},"3":{"en":"anomalous"},"4":{"en":"anomulous"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Anomalous (असामान्य) = deviating from what is standard or expected.</b><br>The correct spelling is “anomalous”: “a-nom-a-lous.”<br><b>Anomaleous</b> inserts an extra “e”; <b>anomallous</b> doubles “l.”<br><b>Anomulous</b> omits “a” before “lous.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): anomalous.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000073271","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Placate</b> [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Soothe"},"2":{"en":"Appease"},"3":{"en":"Infuriate"},"4":{"en":"Calm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Placate (शांत करना) = make someone less angry or hostile.</b><br><b>Soothe (शांत करना)</b> = calm or comfort<br><b>Appease (संतुष्ट करना)</b> = pacify by meeting demands<br><b>Infuriate (क्रोधित करना)</b> = make extremely angry ✔<br><b>Calm (शांत करना)</b> = make tranquil<br>More antonyms: enrage, provoke, antagonize.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Infuriate.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000073272","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the misspelt word. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Winsom"},"2":{"en":"Veneration"},"3":{"en":"Temerity"},"4":{"en":"Supercilious"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Winsome (मनोहर) = attractive or charming.</b><br><b>Winsom</b> omits the final “e”; the correct spelling is “winsome.”<br><b>Veneration (श्रद्धा)</b> = deep respect; spelling correct.<br><b>Temerity (दुःसाहस)</b> = excessive boldness; <b>supercilious (अहंकारी)</b> = haughtily disdainful.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Winsom.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000073273","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of an ancient tear-bottle. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lacrimetory"},"2":{"en":"Lacrymatory"},"3":{"en":"Lacrimattory"},"4":{"en":"Lacrymotory"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Lacrymatory (अश्रु-पात्र) = relating to tears, especially an ancient tear-bottle.</b><br>The accepted spelling in the options is “lacrymatory.”<br><b>Lacrimetory</b> uses “i” and “e” in the wrong positions; <b>Lacrimattory</b> additionally doubles “t.”<br><b>Lacrymotory</b> omits “a” before “tory.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Lacrymatory.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000073274","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “A person who seeks to overthrow established government by unlawful means”. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Anarchist"},"2":{"en":"Immigrant"},"3":{"en":"Diplomat"},"4":{"en":"Patriot"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Anarchist (अराजकतावादी) = a person who seeks to overthrow established government or authority.</b><br><b>Immigrant (आप्रवासी)</b> = a person who comes to live in another country<br><b>Diplomat (राजनयिक)</b> = an official representing a nation<br><b>Patriot (देशभक्त)</b> = a person devoted to their country<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Anarchist.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000073275","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “Habitually dishonest; lying”. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Weracious"},"2":{"en":"Candid"},"3":{"en":"Mendacious"},"4":{"en":"Frank"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Mendacious (झूठा) = habitually dishonest or lying.</b><br><b>Veracious (सत्यवादी)</b> = truthful; the printed “Weracious” is misspelt.<br><b>Candid (स्पष्टवादी)</b> = open and sincere<br><b>Frank (खरा)</b> = direct and honest<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Mendacious.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000073276","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word:<br>The calligrapher added a <b>cadel</b> in the manuscript margin. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The scribe’s cadel resembled a floral spiral."},"2":{"en":"The artist painted a cadel into the decorative header."},"3":{"en":"The engineer adjusted the cadel in the circuit board."},"4":{"en":"The monk illuminated the cadel in gold leaf."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Cadel: an ornamental calligraphic flourish; the same spelling is used differently in option 3.</b><br>The original sentence concerns manuscript decoration.<br>Option 3 places “cadel” in a circuit board, indicating a different technical referent.<br>Options 1, 2 and 4 all retain its calligraphic or decorative meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The engineer adjusted the cadel in the circuit board..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000073277","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>I <b>prefer tea than</b> coffee. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"prefer tea more than"},"2":{"en":"prefer tea for"},"3":{"en":"prefer tea to"},"4":{"en":"prefer tea on"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Prefer X to Y” is the standard comparison.</b><br>Correct sentence: “I <b>prefer tea to</b> coffee.”<br>“More than” is redundant after “prefer”; “for” and “on” are not used in this construction.<br>The preposition “to” introduces the less preferred item.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): prefer tea to.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000073278","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech.<br>She said, “I don't like spicy food.” [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She said she didn’t liked spicy food."},"2":{"en":"She said that she didn't like spicy food."},"3":{"en":"She said she doesn’t like spicy food."},"4":{"en":"She said that she doesn’t liked spicy food."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Backshift present “don’t like” to past “didn’t like.”</b><br>After “didn’t,” the base verb “like” is required.<br>A and D incorrectly use “liked” after an auxiliary.<br>C retains the present tense.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): She said that she didn't like spicy food..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000073279","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech.<br>She said, “I met him yesterday.” [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She said that she met him the day before."},"2":{"en":"She said that she had met him the day before."},"3":{"en":"She said that she has met him the day before."},"4":{"en":"She said that she meets him yesterday."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Backshift simple past to past perfect and “yesterday” to “the day before.”</b><br>“I met” becomes “she had met.”<br>A changes the time phrase but not the tense.<br>C uses present perfect; D retains present tense and “yesterday.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): She said that she had met him the day before..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000073280","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences to form a coherent paragraph:<br>1. The erosion of trust in public institutions is a defining feature of contemporary political discourse, influencing voter behavior and policy outcomes.<br>2. Consequently, robust and transparent governance mechanisms are essential to rebuilding public confidence and ensuring the legitimacy of a democratic system.<br>3. This crisis can be traced to a historical understanding of the “social contract” where the public grants authority in exchange for protection and well-being.<br>4. The breakdown of this unwritten agreement has led to widespread disillusionment and a perception of institutional failure, with significant social consequences. [SSC CGL 09/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2,3,1,4"},"2":{"en":"1,4,3,2"},"3":{"en":"1,3,4,2"},"4":{"en":"3,1,2,4"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 1-3-4-2</b><br>Sentence 1 introduces the erosion of trust, and sentence 3 explains “this crisis” through the social contract.<br>Sentence 4 describes the breakdown of that agreement and its consequences.<br>Sentence 2 concludes with the remedy: transparent governance to rebuild confidence.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1,3,4,2.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};